{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence","id":1038569,"title":"Violence begets violence","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-26T14:16:09-08:00","id":1038569,"title":"Violence begets violence","content":"I know this is a strange place for a rant since while I do post here from time I don't do it a lot. Well I was on facebook and I see that C20 is now available for pre-order and since I didn't get in the Kickstarter I want to pre-order a copy. Now while doing my little dance of joy another WoD friend of mine has been called a Nazi just for saying what the subject says. Now people are calling him bad names and talking how we need to stomp all Nazi in the street. Do people like this not understand that acting like that is no different than what you are fighting against? Heck if you really want to stop engage them in debate especially the most radical idea, because those are the ones that will crumble like a house of cards. Why don't people understand part of the reason we have Free Speech is so that the idiots are exposed to the light of day instead of letting them fester with whispers in back rooms where they can go.<br /> <br /> Oh and the worst part of the story is I still haven't pre-ordered my copy of C20 since I can't decided between the PDF or the Deluxe copy. Decisions can be so hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","name":"JBRocky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T14:38:19-08:00","id":1038587,"title":"","content":"I am sorry that your friend has been unfairly (I assume) called a nazi. But honestly, I can't agree with you that nonviolence is the foolproof solution you make it out to be in this post. The so-called &quot;alt-right&quot; are incredibly skilled at twisting an argument in knots to make themselves appear more reasonable than they are. And at the end of the day, even if you debate circles around a neo-nazi, you've still accomplished nothing to actually put a stop to their spread of hate and misinformation. Ultimately they're still a hateful person who is going to continue propagating violence against others and brainwashing the naive into their way of thinking when you're not there to make them look foolish. Where in World War 2 history were the nazis ever thwarted by civil discourse and logical reasoning? Conversely, direct, physical action gets immediate results. I think I'm safe in assuming this is about Richard Spenser? Cause he has since expressed hesitance to appear in public, which is a 100% positive thing if you ask me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-26-2017, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T15:06:33-08:00","id":1038601,"title":"","content":"If you advocate for genocide, you're gonna get pushback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T15:10:38-08:00","id":1038603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1038587#post1038587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am sorry that your friend has been infairly (I assume) called a nazi. But honestly, I can't agree that need nonviolence is the foolproof solution you make it out to be in this post. The so-called &quot;alt-right&quot; are incredibly skilled at twisting an argument in knots to make themselves appear more reasonable than they are. And at the end of the day, even if you debate circles around a neo-nazi, you've still accomplished nothing to actually put a stop to their spread of hate and misinformation. Ultimately they're still a hateful person who is going to continue propagating violence against others and brainwashing the naive into their way of thinking when you're not there to make them look foolish. Where in World War 2 history were the nazis ever thwarted by civil discourse and logical reasoning? Conversely, direct, physical action gets immediate results. I think I'm safe in assuming this is about Richard Spenser? Cause he has since expressed hesitance to appear in public, which is a 100% positive thing if you ask me.</div> </div> </div> </div> If I am debating a radical I don't see them as my audience, I see the rational people who have not made a decision as my audience. I don't think you can change any radicals mind but you can stop others from going down that path. I have to disagree with you on that one. I like to have the bad people right out front for all to see that way you can keep track of them and know what they are doing. When they hide that is when they are dangerous, that is when they can spread their hate when nobody is listening.<br /> <br /> You are right about how civil discourse did not stop the Nazi's rising to power, but they also used violence to silence those who opposed them. Hence part of the reason I don't like the idea of using violence to silence those we disagree with. It was a tactic both in Germany and Italy and we know how that ended. I guess it's part I don't like the idea that just because that guy did something I can do, if that other guy is scum be better than that.<br /> <br /> I didn't ask if it was about Richard Spenser but you are most likely right, as for Jason (my friend) he is fine and more of a WTF moment instead actually taking offense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","name":"JBRocky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T15:10:39-08:00","id":1038604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1038587#post1038587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am sorry that your friend has been infairly (I assume) called a nazi. But honestly, I can't agree that need nonviolence is the foolproof solution you make it out to be in this post. The so-called &quot;alt-right&quot; are incredibly skilled at twisting an argument in knots to make themselves appear more reasonable than they are. And at the end of the day, even if you debate circles around a neo-nazi, you've still accomplished nothing to actually put a stop to their spread of hate and misinformation.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, if you beat them down or kill them outright, they get to play the &quot;victim&quot; card and further reinforce their message by making <i>you </i>look like the unreasonable one. Which, if you just used violence to resolve an argument, you might well be.<br /> <br /> If peaceful engagement is <i>truly </i>impossible (and you should never assume it isn't before you've tried), the next-best thing is to do an endrun around the crazies and speak to the more reasonable people around them. Hate may be impossible to stamp out completely, but with effort it can be marginalized to the extent that it has a minimal impact on politics or culture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":".  Ninja'd! 01-26-2017, 06:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T15:22:45-08:00","id":1038608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JBRocky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1038603#post1038603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If I am debating a radical I don't see them as my audience, I see the rational people who have not made a decision as my audience. I don't think you can change any radicals mind but you can stop others from going down that path. I have to disagree with you on that one. I like to have the bad people right out front for all to see that way you can keep track of them and know what they are doing. When they hide that is when they are dangerous, that is when they can spread their hate when nobody is listening.<br /> <br /> You are right about how civil discourse did not stop the Nazi's rising to power, but they also used violence to silence those who opposed them. Hence part of the reason I don't like the idea of using violence to silence those we disagree with. It was a tactic both in Germany and Italy and we know how that ended. I guess it's part I don't like the idea that just because that guy did something I can do, if that other guy is scum be better than that.<br /> <br /> I didn't ask if it was about Richard Spenser but you are most likely right, as for Jason (my friend) he is fine and more of a WTF moment instead actually taking offense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I gotcha. I'm certainly not going to condemn anyone for not engaging in violence against nazis. I'd be a hypocrite if I did, as I can't ever see myself punching another person in the face, even scum of the earth like Sean Spenser. By the same token though, I'm not going to condemn the person who did. A good punch in the face is the least thing a man who literally advocates genocide without a shred of irony deserves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T15:45:16-08:00","id":1038619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1038604#post1038604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, if you beat them down or kill them outright, they get to play the &amp;quot;victim&amp;quot; card and further reinforce their message by making <i>you </i>look like the unreasonable one. Which, if you just used violence to resolve an argument, you might well be.<br /> <br /> If peaceful engagement is <i>truly </i>impossible (and you should never assume it isn't before you've tried), the next-best thing is to do an endrun around the crazies and speak to the more reasonable people around them. Hate may be impossible to stamp out completely, but with effort it can be marginalized to the extent that it has a minimal impact on politics or culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole &quot;ignore them because you're above that level of nonsense&quot; got one of them into the White House.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T16:02:43-08:00","id":1038627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1038619#post1038619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole &quot;ignore them because you're above that level of nonsense&quot; got one of them into the White House.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say anything about ignoring them. And I don't think anybody <i>ignored </i>Ol' Donny Boy. But not enough effort was made to try to turn away his more reluctant supporters, either. Remember - he still lost the popular vote. If the Democratic campaign's had been a little stronger and appealed more to voters in swing states, I believe things would be different now. <br /> <br /> Oddly, being in power makes Donny more vulnerable in some ways. Now we can point to his failings as they happen, instead of issuing warnings that were ignored because Trump's supporters rationalized his rhetoric as a temporary thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T16:45:13-08:00","id":1038642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JBRocky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence#post1038569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this is a strange place for a rant since while I do post here from time I don't do it a lot. Well I was on facebook and I see that C20 is now available for pre-order and since I didn't get in the Kickstarter I want to pre-order a copy. Now while doing my little dance of joy another WoD friend of mine has been called a Nazi just for saying what the subject says. Now people are calling him bad names and talking how we need to stomp all Nazi in the street. Do people like this not understand that acting like that is no different than what you are fighting against? Heck if you really want to stop engage them in debate especially the most radical idea, because those are the ones that will crumble like a house of cards. Why don't people understand part of the reason we have Free Speech is so that the idiots are exposed to the light of day instead of letting them fester with whispers in back rooms where they can go.<br /> <br /> Oh and the worst part of the story is I still haven't pre-ordered my copy of C20 since I can't decided between the PDF or the Deluxe copy. Decisions can be so hard.</div> </div> </div> </div>All I know is that the more peaceful and reasonable methods have been tried for decades now and the stupid has just grown. Sometimes, the sledgehammer approach is needed to get the point across. The days when people respected intelligence and a well crafted argument are long gone. Dead and buried beneath such things as reality TV, calling someone an &quot;Einstein&quot; being an insult, and the loudest voice being considered the correct one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 01-26-2017, 07:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T16:49:38-08:00","id":1038647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1038601#post1038601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you advocate for genocide, you're gonna get pushback.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Pretty much.<br /> <br /> No other way around it in my eyes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T17:25:57-08:00","id":1038655,"title":"","content":"It's kind of funny how life is so often a circle.<br /> <br /> Back during the Civil Rights era, white supremacists would often attack liberal marchers and protesters and then defend themselves by saying something like, &quot;Freedom of speech? Sure you have that, but you don't have freedom from consequences. If you say things that piss people off, someone's gonna come over and punch you in the face. That's just how it is, and that's the price you might have to pay for saying something that makes me mad. Open your mouth and speak up at your own risk.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now we have liberals advocating punching white supremacists in the face and basically using that same argument. I can't help but chuckle at the irony of that.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I mean realistically, that's just how it is.<br /> <br /> Simply because you can legally say (almost) anything you want doesn't mean there won't be consequences for what you say, and sometimes those consequences could be in the form of fists or even bullets. Obviously anybody using violence on someone because of what they said is committing a crime, and I suppose you can take comfort in the fact that the law will be on your side - you can have the attacker arrested. But that's still a small comfort to anyone who is intimidated into keeping their mouth shut through the threat of physical violence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T18:06:06-08:00","id":1038667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1038655#post1038655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's kind of funny how life is so often a circle.<br /> <br /> Back during the Civil Rights era, white supremacists would often attack liberal marchers and protesters and then defend themselves by saying something like, &quot;Freedom of speech? Sure you have that, but you don't have freedom from consequences. If you say things that piss people off, someone's gonna come over and punch you in the face. That's just how it is, and that's the price you might have to pay for saying something that makes me mad. Open your mouth and speak up at your own risk.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now we have liberals advocating punching white supremacists in the face and basically using that same argument. I can't help but chuckle at the irony of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference is, only one of these groups is made up of people who actively advocate for genocide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T18:25:43-08:00","id":1038675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1038667#post1038667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difference is, only one of these groups is made up of people who actively advocate for genocide.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome to justify it however you like, but at the end of the day, it comes down to defending the use of violence against someone for saying things you don't care for. And that is a <i>very</i> dangerous road to go down, wherein people begin trying to legitimize violence as a way to stifle speech.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, at least in the US, physically attacking people who advocate for genocide (or gay rights or any other position) is a crime, and hopefully anyone who <i>does</i> use violence or the threat of violence to try and stifle someone else's free speech, no matter whether how deplorable it may be, is arrested and punished in a court of law.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T18:43:35-08:00","id":1038680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1038675#post1038675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're welcome to justify it however you like, but at the end of the day, it comes down to defending the use of violence against someone for saying things you don't care for. And that is a <i>very</i> dangerous road to go down, wherein people begin trying to legitimize violence as a way to stifle speech.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, at least in the US, physically attacking people who advocate for genocide (or gay rights or any other position) is a crime, and hopefully anyone who <i>does</i> use violence or the threat of violence to try and stifle someone else's free speech, no matter whether how deplorable it may be, is arrested and punished in a court of law.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this IMO.<br /> <br /> Speech is free in the US, the government shouldn't have the ability to clamp down on it, nor through inaction against criminal activity allow it to be suppressed. <br /> <br /> That means I don't support him getting punched for what he says. Now, if he does something illegal, I fully support the idea of tossing his ass in jail for as long as reasonably possible.<br /> <br /> I *really* don't like the argument &quot;He promotes Nazi beliefs with bad logic and reasoning, therefore he's part of the Nazis from 60 years ago therefore I get to punch him.&quot; The Nazis of WWII are dead (well apart from a handful that are probably still alive). They were violent and were countered with violence... AFTER they started the violence. It's the time gap and order of action/reaction.<br /> <br /> Or to put it another way attacking him because he spews vile filth, because the country/world is better off without him can be rephrased to &quot;We must purge this filth from our streets to have a good, right, just and strong society.&quot; Which pretty much IS the kind of thing the Nazis would state.<br /> <br /> <br /> All that having been said, I *also* fully support and encourage businesses and individuals to exercise their right to refuse to serve people in his case.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T18:51:55-08:00","id":1038682,"title":"","content":"Inciting genocide is against the law as well. Spencer goes around it by advocating for a 'white only' nation without really suggesting a way to get there while also going on and on about how horrible 'certain people' are.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth I don't believe he should have been punched. It's against the law to begin with, but I think, especially with one as tapped into the internet as Spencer, it would only create more followers for him. People who might not have fallen for his rhetoric might think what he says deserves a second chance.<br /> <br /> That said we don't know who the puncher is and he's made, through proxies, threats against specific individuals, it could be one of them getting revenge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-26-2017, 09:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T18:56:20-08:00","id":1038685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1038675#post1038675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're welcome to justify it however you like, but at the end of the day, it comes down to defending the use of violence against someone for saying things you don't care for. And that is a <i>very</i> dangerous road to go down, wherein people begin trying to legitimize violence as a way to stifle speech.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, at least in the US, physically attacking people who advocate for genocide (or gay rights or any other position) is a crime, and hopefully anyone who <i>does</i> use violence or the threat of violence to try and stifle someone else's free speech, no matter whether how deplorable it may be, is arrested and punished in a court of law.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a big difference between &quot;saying things I don't care for&quot; and trying to incite mass murder on a global scale. I don't think a slippery slope argument holds up here when hate speech, and particularly hate speech that advocates for mass violence, is easily identifiable and separable from other forms of speech. As Justice Frank Murphy said, &quot;<span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">There are certain well-defined and limited classes of speech, the prevention and punishment of which have never been thought to raise a Constitutional problem. These include the lewd and obscene, the profane, the libelous and the insulting or 'fighting' words \u2013 those which by their very utterances inflict injury or tend to incite an immediate breach of the peace.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, the SCOTUS might not consider Spencer's speech at significant risk of &quot;inciting imminent lawless action and is likely to incite or produce such action&quot;, and it's certainly debatable how immediate the risk is and whether its immediacy justifies recourse. But at the end of the day, I'm not going to lose sleep over someone getting hurt for spouting fighting words.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T18:59:23-08:00","id":1038687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1038680#post1038680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I *really* don't like the argument &quot;He promotes Nazi beliefs with bad logic and reasoning, therefore he's part of the Nazis from 60 years ago therefore I get to punch him.&quot; The Nazis of WWII are dead (well apart from a handful that are probably still alive). They were violent and were countered with violence... AFTER they started the violence. It's the time gap and order of action/reaction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, I think whether or not you want to call him a nazi makes no practical difference. Advocating genocide is advocating genocide, no matter what decade it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1038680#post1038680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or to put it another way attacking him because he spews vile filth, because the country/world is better off without him can be rephrased to &quot;We must purge this filth from our streets to have a good, right, just and strong society.&quot; Which pretty much IS the kind of thing the Nazis would state.</div> </div> </div> </div>But there is a difference when the &quot;filth&quot; the quote refers to is &quot;everyone of a certain race&quot; and when it refers to &quot;people who genuinely want to murder everyone of a certain race.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-26-2017, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T19:02:11-08:00","id":1038689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1038687#post1038687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, I think whether or not you want to call him a nazi makes no practical difference. Advocating genocide is advocating genocide, no matter what decade it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but again no matter what decade it is, it should be handled by the law if it is illegal and NOT someone randomly assaulting him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T19:05:03-08:00","id":1038692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1038689#post1038689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but again no matter what decade it is, it should be handled by the law if it is illegal and NOT someone randomly assaulting him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. I wouldn't have done it. But I'm not going to get upset that someone else did or pretend he didn't deserve it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T19:09:48-08:00","id":1038695,"title":"","content":"I'm not going to shed any tears for a white supremacist getting punched either. I just find it a bit ironic that the same group of people that used to get beat up by white supremacists are now repeating the same sorts of justifications while beating up white supremacists.<br /> <br /> Regardless, hopefully assaulting people for the things they say, no matter how upsetting, remains illegal and anyone who does attack Richard Spencer for the things he says (or who attacks members of <i>any</i> group with the purpose of stifling their speech) is promptly arrested and put through the court system. In the US, even if someone says the most profane words about the things you hold dearest to your heart, if you decide to punch him for that, legally you're in the wrong. And that's a good thing.<br /> <br /> I, at least, would not want to live in a country where people can use the threat of violent reprisals to try and stifle what someone else wants to say or write, even if I disagree with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T19:53:10-08:00","id":1038714,"title":"","content":"Oh but the slippery slope does hold up here. What is the deciding factor on who gets attacked next? Is it hate speech? Anyone can decide something is hate speech and call a person a Racist, Bigot, Sexist, or what ever term they want, and that is justification to attack them? That is the slippery slope, since when you have decided it's ok to use violence against people, what is to stop them from doing the same against you?<br /> <br /> Now I don't like Richard Spencer and his white supremacist group. I also don't like the person who attacked him and the Anarcho-syndicalism group that formed the Black Bloc in DC. <br /> <br /> Talking about the threat of Violence against a person you disagree with. This might be a Milo Yiannopoulis but it is still a girl who is threatened for just holding a sign after they take it from her. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Il3qTuwvH3g\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Il3qTuwvH3g</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9486,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","user":"JBRocky","date":". 01-26-2017, 11:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","name":"JBRocky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T20:00:47-08:00","id":1038720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JBRocky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1038714#post1038714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh but the slippery slope does hold up here.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really seems like more of an isolated incident. Not all liberals are saying it's alright and something to be done. In your friends case, I think they were the subject of name-calling because they expressed a statement that disagreed with a group they were talking to, not because there's suddenly bands of liberals asking people if they approve and labeling them Nazi if they say no on their way to the next fascist to assault. Even if their statement was meant more as a middle ground, 'See what this can lead to.'<br /> <br /> Was the incident they were involved with online? Because the cliquishness of online communities may have contributed to it. A classroom of some sort would be my second guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-26-2017, 11:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T20:32:52-08:00","id":1038737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1038720#post1038720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It really seems like more of an isolated incident. Not all liberals are saying it's alright and something to be done. In your friends case, I think they were the subject of name-calling because they expressed a statement that disagreed with a group they were talking to, not because there's suddenly bands of liberals asking people if they approve and labeling them Nazi if they say no on their way to the next fascist to assault. Even if their statement was meant more as a middle ground, 'See what this can lead to.'<br /> <br /> Was the incident they were involved with online? Because the cliquishness of online communities may have contributed to it. A classroom of some sort would be my second guess.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh agreed 100% but I am more worried about people who think violence is ok. When do we as a nation decide to concentrate on what we have in common instead of looking for reason to hate each other. When do we tell the radicals on both sides that enough is enough. I guess the whole thing boils down to I am not worried that they called him a Nazi but that they believed it is ok to attack people that think different and that all you need to do is label someone and not they are the enemy and you can now attack them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","name":"JBRocky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T20:50:18-08:00","id":1038741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JBRocky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1038737#post1038737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh agreed 100% but I am more worried about people who think violence is ok. When do we as a nation decide to concentrate on what we have in common instead of looking for reason to hate each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>More like 'when do we as a species,' this is hardly confined to America. There are people all over the world hating and killing each other for what others might think of as the smallest of things, and there always have been.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When do we tell the radicals on both sides that enough is enough. I guess the whole thing boils down to I am not worried that they called him a Nazi but that they believed it is ok to attack people that think different and that all you need to do is label someone and not they are the enemy and you can now attack them. </div> </div> </div>Was your friend attacked? They name-called, but if they really believed he was a Nazi, and that it was okay to hit Nazis, wouldn't they have assaulted him? Maybe they were just caught up in their argument.<br /> <br /> For most people talk doesn't lead immediately to action, and I suppose you should be thankful that in much of the world we have things that can help us ameliorate our attitudes, whether they be distractions, the words of others or the fear of punishment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-26-2017, 11:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T21:05:15-08:00","id":1038746,"title":"","content":"Nah Jason was never attacked, but I do believe they at least considered him just as horrible as one if not an actual Nazi one himself. I also highly doubt anyone was caught up in an argument since Jason is very laid back and sometimes you need to poke him to make sure he is alive, so it was most likely just a simple discussion, but then I was not there so I really don't know. But it still comes down to the fact that more and more people are resorting to violence when they don't agree with people, and even more think it is ok. It's not about one isolated incident but that person is different than I am so I am now justified to attack him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","name":"JBRocky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T21:17:07-08:00","id":1038752,"title":"","content":"That person <i>actually wants to kill all of the black people</i>. I think the gravity of that gets lost a bit when we call it &quot;is different than I am.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T21:56:18-08:00","id":1038765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1038752#post1038752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That person <i>actually wants to kill all of the black people</i>. I think the gravity of that gets lost a bit when we call it &quot;is different than I am.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but he's not actually out there killing anyone.<br /> <br /> People can think and say whatever the hell they want and should be able to do so without having to be overly worried about getting the crap beat out of them. I don't like Nazi's. I don't like members of NAMBLA. I don't like religious conservatives who want to throw gay people in concentration camps. But I also don't think we should be punching those people merely because they give voice to their beliefs and opinions, no matter how horrific they are.<br /> <br /> On the scale of morality, the guy who physically assaults someone for saying or thinking something that's terrible is worse than the guy who was merely saying or thinking something terrible. That's why punching someone is a crime while saying you want to kill black people (or legalize pedophilia, or put gays in camps or whatever) is not criminal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T23:36:10-08:00","id":1038781,"title":"","content":"Yeah not losing sleep over the off center lovetap that he received. If other people want to moralize about the situation that is their own business but this isn't really comparable to systematic issues of violence in America, like say the ones BLM is fighting against. One is an incident, the other is system and that is a massively important distinction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T09:26:23-08:00","id":1038939,"title":"","content":"Nazis need punching. I don't know if your friend needs punching or not, seeing as I have no idea who they are, but if he is, well, Nazis need punching.<br /> <br /> When decades of peaceable attempts have fostered a crueler, subtler oppression, the only answer is a blunt one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T09:59:30-08:00","id":1038956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1038939#post1038939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nazis need punching. I don't know if your friend needs punching or not, seeing as I have no idea who they are, but if he is, well, Nazis need punching.<br /> <br /> When decades of peaceable attempts have fostered a crueler, subtler oppression, the only answer is a blunt one.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK. Supposing, hypothetically, that I take this comment <i>very</i> badly. I take it as proof that you are some kind of monster for advocating violence against people who haven't actually done you any measurable harm. And then suppose I decide that the correct response to this is to pre-emptively attack you in order to prevent you from doing... whatever it is I thought you were going to do (punch anyone you arbitrarily declare to be a Nazi, perhaps?).<br /> <br /> Would that be in any way just? The number of assumptions I need to make to justify this course of action by itself should give a reasonable person pause. And who am I to decide who is dangerous, or what level of violence is an acceptable response, anyway?<br /> <br /> It's one thing to fight back against someone who is <i>presently or about to </i>attack you or people you care about. It's quite another to assume someone is dangerous and escalate conflict with them just because you don't like what they say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 01-27-2017, 01:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T10:16:09-08:00","id":1038965,"title":"","content":"You taking it badly is not what I would call my problem. There are larger issues to be prepared for.<br /> <br /> I don't need people to harm me. People having been dealing with a staggering increase in violence since they realized they were validated by the election. They are hurting people already, and me preparing myself to just be calm and rational about isn't going to stop them from hurting people. The only response is to provide a consequence. The only response is to have people prepare for how they'll make &quot;No More&quot; loud and clear. I don't need people to harm me. Hell, I'm fucking safe. But they will still hurt other people. That's why I need to decide here and now that I will come out swinging.<br /> <br /> Is it just? Sure it is. Is it legal? Nope. But have these people hidden safely behind the legal system for decades? Yep. Are they going to manipulate it to keep themselves while they keep hurting people on a scale I'll never be able to operate at? Yep.<br /> <br /> Is it irrational to have a pre-escalated response to disagreements of this nature that incorporate violence? Sure. Are the people I am proposing violence against in any way interested in rational? Nope. Are these people the ones enforcing the status quo of harm against masses of people who don't deserve it? Yep.<br /> <br /> If you decide that's worth punching me over, well then. Stand By Your Convictions.<br /> <br /> In the mean time, I've made a decision that I'm not going to let people think that their harm is not watched, and not responded to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T10:20:06-08:00","id":1038967,"title":"","content":"I maintain that anyone who is mad about a Nazi getting punched is free to apologize to them. If they do then they get to freely admit that they are a better person than I am by apologizing to a Nazi. If that's not something they can bring themselves to do then I really don't want to hear any moral posturing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T10:28:58-08:00","id":1038972,"title":"","content":"Like, seriously, I've done the entire &quot;you don't break the cycle by violence&quot; thing. I've done &quot;Discourse and understanding are the way forward.&quot; By and large, I still believe in that. THat is more my default than &quot;Punch Nazis.&quot;<br /> <br /> But I have dealt with too many people who aren't going to listen. I've dealt with people who say they'll see what you want to show them, and then weasel out of it time and again because really they just think you're wrong. It <i>happens</i>.<br /> <br /> Those are the people maintaining the current status quo. Those are the people allowing harm to happen.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. I've played the soft game. It can work. But there are people and places and times where it doesn't, and the only answers there are a) Let them keep on hurting others, or b) <i>do something about it</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T10:44:18-08:00","id":1038976,"title":"","content":"Exactly. I believe in civil discourse, civil disobedience, civil everything really*. If civility is all you have though you're going to have a bad time when you find out it isn't all-powerful.<br /> <br /> *(Just don't get me started on those &quot;Choose Civility&quot; stickers)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T11:07:41-08:00","id":1038985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1038972#post1038972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, yeah. I've played the soft game. It can work. But there are people and places and times where it doesn't, and the only answers there are a) Let them keep on hurting others, or b) <i>do something about it</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. Let's talk about some nonviolent approaches to option B.<br /> <br /> 1. Deprive the target of money by turning their customers/clients/investors off them.<br /> 2. Deprive the target of social influence by damaging their reputation, connections, venues, or partners.<br /> 3. Directly attack the target through the legal system by suing them or by inviting suits from them that they cannot win.<br /> 4. Deprive the target of power by forcing adjustments to whatever policies/laws/regulations they are exploiting.<br /> \u200b5. Do any of the above to people close to the target - friends, family, allies in the community.<br /> <br /> If you're determined that you've got to punish someone to deter them or neutralize them, there's a lot of ways to mess people up without ever laying a hand on them. Words are almost as deadly as guns, if you say them in the right way at the right time to the right person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 01-27-2017, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T11:31:25-08:00","id":1039006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1038956#post1038956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK. Supposing, hypothetically, that I take this comment <i>very</i> badly. I take it as proof that you are some kind of monster for advocating violence against people who haven't actually done you any measurable harm. And then suppose I decide that the correct response to this is to pre-emptively attack you in order to prevent you from doing... whatever it is I thought you were going to do (punch anyone you arbitrarily declare to be a Nazi, perhaps?).<br /> <br /> Would that be in any way just? The number of assumptions I need to make to justify this course of action by itself should give a reasonable person pause. And who am I to decide who is dangerous, or what level of violence is an acceptable response, anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is indeed a lot of assumptions you have to make to reach the conclusion that Sean is a dangerous person arbitrarily calling people nazies and then punching them for it. A lot more assumptions than it takes to reach the conclusion that Richard Spenser is a dangerous person trying to rally support for the genocide of black people. In fact, you don't need to make any assumptions at all to reach the latter conclusion, because he has publicly stated as much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1038956#post1038956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's one thing to fight back against someone who is <i>presently or about to </i>attack you or people you care about. It's quite another to assume someone is dangerous and escalate conflict with them just because you don't like what they say.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its not a matter of not liking what someone says. It's a matter of not tolerating advocacy for mass extermination of human beings. It takes zero assumptions to know that someone who earnestly says we should kill all the black people is dangerous.<br /> <br /> This isn't about &quot;let's go beat up anybody we decide is a nazi.&quot; It's about &quot;this person is actively attempting to incite global mass violence and extermination, he really deserves to be clocked.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T11:33:39-08:00","id":1039010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1038985#post1038985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Words are almost as deadly as guns</div> </div> </div> </div>If you honestly believe this, then why on earth would you support someone trying to use words to get an entire race of people killed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-27-2017, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T12:12:15-08:00","id":1039033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, yeah. I've played the soft game. It can work. But there are people and places and times where it doesn't, and the only answers there are a) Let them keep on hurting others, or b) <i>do something about it</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, Might Makes It Right? .<br /> <br /> Now, I think there's something fundamentally flawed in using violence agains't someone that's all bark but no bite. Not listening it's hardly something that deserves punishment, unless you want a &quot;Thought Police&quot; controling what's right to think and what isn't. In which case, <i>woe for those that have the least Might, because those are the ones that are going to be suffering all the punching</i>. That's the problem of violence, it never end well for the weak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-27-2017, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T12:13:37-08:00","id":1039035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1039006#post1039006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is indeed a lot of assumptions you have to make to reach the conclusion that Sean is a dangerous person arbitrarily calling people nazies and then punching them for it. A lot more assumptions than it takes to reach the conclusion that Richard Spenser is a dangerous person trying to rally support for the genocide of black people. In fact, you don't need to make any assumptions at all to reach the latter conclusion, because he has publicly stated as much.</div> </div> </div> </div>In fairness, I haven't wasted a lot of words on the nuance arriving here. A lot of people here have a long knowledge of me, so reading something like that has context for most people. You read it straight up, and it's unfailingly unapologetic, which is kind of unnecessarily cold and sharp. It doesn't help that I've neither a) clarified who I thinks needs to be punched, and b) basically told the OP that his friend, who probably did end up on the wrong side of a conversation, would deserve it if he was a Nazi.<br /> <br /> Clearly, no, violence isn't the answer for everything. I am not some punching machine out to punch all the people who only slightly align with perpetuating the harmful system that exists and is rapidly growing right now. But I think there's a clear delineation that can be reached between someone who might be aligned with that system but can be swayed over, and those who have decided to set themselves firmly with it, and beyond that there's a difference between people who merely align with it and those who have the power to put things forward.<br /> <br /> At the heart of this is a tough lesson I've had to learn. In an ideal world, violence wouldn't ever be needed. Even in the reality we deal with, reaching a state of violence means that a failure has been achieved. But the truth of the matter is that, yeah, there's a time and place where violence is the answer. It's a dangerous and scary thought, because it;s the beginning of a lot of slippery slopes to becoming a monster. It's tough to say when is the time for it or who has the authority to make that decision, and the consequences of those decisions, and the limits of any answer given.<br /> <br /> But at the end of the day, there is a time when violence is the answer. And while not perfect, Nazis Need Punching seems like a decent ruling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T12:18:44-08:00","id":1039039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1039006#post1039006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't about &quot;let's go beat up anybody we decide is a nazi.&quot; It's about &quot;this person is actively attempting to incite global mass violence and extermination, he really deserves to be clocked.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If he was <i>really</i> inciting global mass violence and extermination, he'd be subject to punishment for incitement. We have the <a href=\"http://freespeechdebate.com/en/case/the-brandenburg-test-for-incitement-to-violence/\" target=\"_blank\">Brandenburg test</a> for just this reason. Find a direct connection between someone's words and a specific crime committed, or a specific crime suggested, and you have your case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1039010#post1039010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you honestly believe this, then why on earth would you support someone trying to use words to get an entire race of people killed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't confuse &quot;refusing to commit violence against&quot; with &quot;support.&quot;<br /> <br /> I do this because I believe that building a counter-consensus against hate speech and prosecuting hate crimes is more effective and has fewer deleterious side-effects than punching people I want to shut up. It's also slower and more effortful, but that's the price we have to pay for lasting change.<br /> <br /> To be clear, I <i>do not believe we have reached the &quot;Nazi&quot; threshold. </i>There is not a gang of jackbooted zealots roaming the countryside, murdering anyone who doesn't conform to their ideals. <i>If</i> that happens, then it will be time to put away the pen and take up the sword. But not before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 01-27-2017, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T12:22:05-08:00","id":1039040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1039033#post1039033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Might Makes It Right? .<br /> <br /> Now, I think there's something fundamentally flawed in using violence agains't someone that's all bark but no bite. Not listening it's hardly something that deserves punishment, unless you want a &quot;Thought Police&quot; controling what's right to say and what isn't. In which case, <i>woe for those that have the least Might, because those are the ones that are going to be suffering all the punching</i>. That's the problem of violence, it nevers end well for the weak.</div> </div> </div> </div>For context, consider that I weigh a buck thirty. Like, just let that sink in.<br /> <br /> (I mean, also for context, we should mention that I was constantly getting into fights for half my life as well, not all of them justified, in fairness)<br /> <br /> No, Might does not make right, but Right Sometimes Needs Might. If you believe in law enforcement of any sort, you believe that. And having had the shit beaten out of me as well as having beaten the shit out of others, let me tell you that you'd be surprised how both parties are much more willing to work things out through talking afterwards. It <i>happens</i>.<br /> <br /> But also on point, I don't care if I am being tyrannical by punching Nazis, because Nazis are already being tyrannical.<br /> <br /> The fight is already started. They have thrown the first punch. Hell, they threw several of them, and we could not talk them down from it. What am I supposed to do? Keep asking please while they hurt people who don't deserve it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T12:22:58-08:00","id":1039042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1039033#post1039033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I think there's something fundamentally flawed in using violence agains't someone that's all bark but no bite.</div> </div> </div> </div>The people we're talking about here do have bite. Worse, they're intelligent and selective in their employment of biting, and know how to bark enough to get those who are less judicious about when to bite into a biting mood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T12:24:55-08:00","id":1039043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1039040#post1039040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fight is already started. They have thrown the first punch. Hell, they threw several of them, and we could not talk them down from it. What am I supposed to do? Keep asking please while they hurt people who don't deserve it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Apply pepper spray and tasers to the people doing the punching, not the ones doing the talking.<br /> <br /> I feel like we're talking past each other here. I came into this thread to talk about movements and group posture. You're talking about, what, how to stop hate crimes in progress?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 01-27-2017, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T12:28:28-08:00","id":1039045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1039043#post1039043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apply pepper spray and tasers to the people doing the punching, not the ones doing the talking.<br /> <br /> I feel like we're talking past each other here. I came into this thread to talk about movements and group posture. You're talking about, what, how to stop hate crimes in progress?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on who's talking.<br /> <br /> And I'm talking about the systems and culture that permit the hate crimes that is rapidly becoming the nature of the state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T12:32:03-08:00","id":1039050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fight is already started. They have thrown the first punch. Hell, they threw several of them, and we could not talk them down from it. What am I supposed to do? Keep asking please while they hurt people who don't deserve it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you agree in that violence begets violence...<br /> <br /> If I'm distrustfull of violence, it's because I always assume that I, and the people I care for, are weaker than the &quot;bad guys&quot;. It's arrogant to think that &quot;the good guys&quot; are going to win. That's why we have laws where punching (the remanants) of nazis it's violently punished, (unless it's self defense and yada yada). It's because violence needs to be controled. Otherwise we will act like vikings.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T12:39:32-08:00","id":1039052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1038972#post1038972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, yeah. I've played the soft game. It can work. But there are people and places and times where it doesn't, and the only answers there are a) Let them keep on hurting others, or b) <i>do something about it</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just keep one thing in mind. If the goal of punching white supremacists is simply about personal self-satisfaction and about being able to pat yourself on the back and say, &quot;I sure did something,&quot; that's fine, or if you just want to take a bit of pleasure in seeing a nasty guy get clobbered in the face, that's cool too. <br /> <br /> But if the goal is to actually stop white supremacists from speaking their ideology, then it's important to realize that merely punching them in the face <i>isn't going to stop them.</i> There are a lot who have enough conviction in their ideals that you can't expect to simply bully or terrorize them into being quiet, and every attempt to use violence to shut them down will merely reaffirm their beliefs. <br /> <br /> We've seen plenty of movements throughout history; simple violence and physical assault wasn't enough to stop them, and it won't be enough to stop die-hard white supremacists from talking about their beliefs either. Furthermore white supremacists are often big fans of the Second Amendment so attempts to physically intimidate them will only be able to go so far.<br /> <br /> So if we've decided that you can't stop white supremacists from saying what they believe with words, and history suggests that you won't be able to stop them from saying what they believe with your fists, what's the next step in the attempt to silence white supremacists from talking about their beliefs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T12:42:22-08:00","id":1039053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1039050#post1039050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then you agree in that violence begets violence...<br /> <br /> If I'm distrustfull of violence, it's because I always assume that I, and the people I care for, are weaker than the &quot;bad guys&quot;. It's arrogant to think that &quot;the good guys&quot; are going to win. That's why we have laws where punching (the remanants) of nazis it's violently punished, (unless it's self defense and yada yada). It's because violence needs to be controled. Otherwise we will act like vikings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, violence begets violence. But also, sometimes we do live in world where it's needed. Welcome to our world, it's cruel.<br /> <br /> And I'm distrustful of violence because it has destroyed my life and the lives of several people who didn't deserve it, at my hand. I have spent years divorcing myself from that, chasing an ideal. I still do. I don't want to hurt anyone.<br /> <br /> But the reality of the matter is that we don't live in a world where you can softly correct imbalances. This previous year, in America and Britain, has proved that so fucking hard. You need to shove and push, and yes, punch, to correct the mistakes.<br /> <br /> There's a way to break the cycle of violence, I believe there has to be. I believe non-violence is the best of answers.<br /> <br /> But people are getting hurt now after decades of people trying, and just because I hope for my ideal doesn't mean I'm going to Let Shit Stand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T12:43:08-08:00","id":1039054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1039039#post1039039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If he was <i>really</i> inciting global mass violence and extermination, he'd be subject to punishment for incitement. We have the <a href=\"http://freespeechdebate.com/en/case/the-brandenburg-test-for-incitement-to-violence/&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Brandenburg test</a> for just this reason. Find a direct connection between someone's words and a specific crime committed, or a specific crime suggested, and you have your case.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am aware of the Brandenburg Test, and frankly, I think it's too permissive of speech intended to incite violence and other illegal activity. Particularly with regard to its emphasis on immediacy, because &quot;lets kill all the black people, but not until we have enough power to make sure we can really get it done&quot; is in my opinion no better than &quot;let's kill all the black people right now.&quot; In fact, the former is far more dangerous, in no small part because it's defended by constitutional law.<br /> <br /> And again, I'm not about to go punch anyone over it, but I'm also not going to pretend I don't think the person who did the punching didn't do a good thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1039039#post1039039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't confuse &quot;refusing to commit violence against&quot; with &quot;support.&quot;<br /> <br /> I do this because I believe that building a counter-consensus against hate speech and prosecuting hate crimes is more effective and has fewer deleterious side-effects than punching people I want to shut up. It's also slower and more effortful, but that's the price we have to pay for lasting change.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my opinion, part of building a counter-consensus against hate speech is acknowledging that someone who spews it getting punched is not such a bad thing. Does that mean we should all go around beating up anyone who says anything we don't like? Of course not. But it does mean that when we can all agree that someone wjo is advocating for genocide gets a knuckle sandwich, our response should be &quot;Eh. He had it coming.&quot; instead of &quot;he had a right to say those things because they weren't directly and immediately harming anyone, and the guy who punched him for ir should be in jail.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1039039#post1039039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be clear, I <i>do not believe we have reached the &quot;Nazi&quot; threshold. </i>There is not a gang of jackbooted zealots roaming the countryside, murdering anyone who doesn't conform to their ideals. <i>If</i> that happens, then it will be time to put away the pen and take up the sword. But not before.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree. But I do think we're getting there, and in the mean time we shouldn't be defending the people we can all see are gearing up for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-27-2017, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T13:21:53-08:00","id":1039077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1039050#post1039050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'm distrustfull of violence, it's because I always assume that I, and the people I care for, are weaker than the &quot;bad guys&quot;. It's arrogant to think that &quot;the good guys&quot; are going to win. That's why we have laws where punching (the remanants) of nazis it's violently punished, (unless it's self defense and yada yada). It's because violence needs to be controled. Otherwise we will act like vikings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've had to think about this a lot lately, and its a testament to these times that its a topic I've actually had to lose sleep over. I fear what will happen if violence gets out of control, because innocent people and people I care about will be hurt. People who can't defend themselves. The problem is that the &quot;bad guys&quot; want to hurt people regardless. Innocent people. People I care about. People who can't defend themselves. Right now we have the benefit of institutions to prevent that from happening. Right now. Those institutions are built upon state violence though, and it is the stated goals of the &quot;bad guys&quot; to eventually bend those same institutions, the power of state violence, to hurt people. It's happened before, it can happen again, and if you take a hard look around it is perilously close to happening right now. Its not there yet, and maybe violence will only make things worse, but a lack of violence will not guarantee that the &quot;bad guys&quot; lose. In that calculus we're damned if we do and damned if we don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T13:50:48-08:00","id":1039090,"title":"","content":"While I've been hesitant to join this one (I think most of you can safely assume why), I'm giving in.<br /> <br /> There's a saying I like when thinking about the cycle of violence: &quot;The sword comes into the world because of justice delayed, and justice denied.&quot; This means that, like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> I find the Brandenburg test insufficient for the service of justice. It delays the application of justice, which will only lead to the need for force and violence later. We cannot prevent violence by delaying justice for those speech is meant to harm because the harm is not immediate. We can only delay things.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Nazi threshold standard,&quot; to me sounds a lot like, &quot;Oh good, I might die before people care about doing anything.&quot; Remember that the US Civil War was not started to end slavery and make black people equal, and WWII was not started to stop the genocide of innocent minorities. Those were causes that were added to the propaganda of one side to prop up their moral arguments for their staying in the fight. Lincoln might have thought slavery was a moral wrong, but he still thought that black people were an inferior race. The Allies might have said slaughtering non-combatants was wrong, but that didn't stop them from denying refugees safety from the Nazis or killing German civilians. If we hit this supposed Nazi threshold, it means we've already failed people (and I'm in one of the groups that Nazis like to target).<br /> <br /> For me Nazi rhetorical is not some hypothetical harm either. When someone advocates for Nazi ideology, it is psychologically traumatic to me, because they're saying that I'm subhuman, that people that treat me nicely are bad, and that people that torture me and put me to forced labor until I die are saints. They're saying that because they know it hurts me.<br /> <br /> And yes, I know there's usually some point about how it's just words and I'm giving them that power over me, blah, blah, blah. Screw that. I might have those tools now as an adult. I didn't have those tools as a kid while I sat in fear of being seen while Neo-Nazi's loudly proclaimed their desire to harm people like me on a public bus, and nobody did jack shit; not even ask them to stop. That trauma doesn't just up and disappear to let me blow off Nazi shitheels talking shit now.<br /> <br /> If someone was around to punch one of those assholes, well which is the lesser evil? Some skinhead getting decked, or a scared 12 year old not being traumatized for life because they saw that random strangers that didn't have to do anything standing up and doing something? Which is the worse ripple effect? A trio of Nazis realizing that a bus full of mostly white people like the idea of them getting punched more than they like them talking about beating up non-white people and Jews, or all the better things I never did because I was constantly struggling with trust issues after seeing that busload of people ignore it just like normal German people ignored the Nazis that would eventually come for my family?<br /> <br /> Does violence beget violence? Sort of. But sometimes speech is violence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 01-27-2017, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T14:24:11-08:00","id":1039105,"title":"","content":"^And that is why I'm preparing myself to punch Nazis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T14:37:18-08:00","id":1039115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1039105#post1039105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">^And that is why I'm preparing myself to punch Nazis.</div> </div> </div> </div>While that's probably just typical Internet Bravado, if you do decide to go around attacking people, make sure to pick your targets carefully. Many white supremacists are big fans of the Second Amendment, and assaulting a guy with a gun can easily end up with someone in a coffin. Even if the white supremacist is later arrested and sentenced for escalating the situation, that would probably be of small comfort to your friends and family if you ended up committing &quot;suicide by Nazi.&quot; So double check to make sure he's not armed before throwing your punch. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-27-2017, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T14:41:36-08:00","id":1039117,"title":"","content":"<br /> The cicle of violence cannot stop while we are independant physical animals that desire what other people has, however we went a long way, from tribal people that had to know how to fight because they were always warring, to having countries in wich you aren't necessarily dead because you don't know how to fight. This it's a definite advance in the right way, but it depends on a few people having the power, the violence, to control all other violence. As the Leviatan of Hobbs, we need violence, controled violence.<br /> I'm from a country that has sufferend institucionalized violence from dictatorial goverments, so I know it isn't good to give all the power to the Law (qui custodiet ipsos custodes?). Even then. I think it's worse to think you can go a lo Punisher, sending bullets into &quot;the bad guys heads&quot;, because then it becomes a battle of bands, which it's no different from the tribes that were constantly warring. <hr /><br /> You know what. I couldn't care less what happened to this nazi guy I didn't know, but what does make me loose sleep it's Righteous America deciding my country needs a bit of Freedom(tm). This it's why this topic picked my interest. And don't try to evade the ball! , While politicians are in the war bussiness for money, they're not the ones firing the guns!.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.dailymotion.com/video/xqrtdn_team-america-world-police-clip-action-montage_shortfilms\" data-code=\"xqrtdn\" data-provider=\"dailymotion\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> There are reasons of why USA it's seen as a self-righteous warmongering nation, and there's many reasons of why that attitude it's nearly universaly reviled...<br /> <br /> Righteousness is not different from fanaticism, in the sense that the righteous people are going to defend their posture no matter what, without caring about limmits. Since self impossed limmits are the key to stop violence from happening, we may need to stop being so righteous.<br /> <br /> Also, this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've seen plenty of movements throughout history; simple violence and physical assault wasn't enough to stop them, and it won't be enough to stop die-hard white supremacists from talking about their beliefs either.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can kill the people, but not the IDEA. This it's how democracy survived dictatorship after dictatorship, despite being unable to fight back. In the end, Democracy was bound to return. The idea it's a die hard bitch that can only be diminished with more and more people accepting that it's wrong. You can't do this with violence.<br /> And we should really listen to the alt-right, because you need to know what your enemy thinks, in order to be preppared to battle it with words. I've seen more than one time that the left it's left without arguments, because they just assume that &quot;they're right&quot; (Damn, that sounded like a damn pun, it wasn't intended).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-27-2017, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T17:01:44-08:00","id":1039164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1039115#post1039115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While that's probably just typical Internet Bravado, if you do decide to go around attacking people, make sure to pick your targets carefully. Many white supremacists are big fans of the Second Amendment, and assaulting a guy with a gun can easily end up with someone in a coffin. Even if the white supremacist is later arrested and sentenced for escalating the situation, that would probably be of small comfort to your friends and family if you ended up committing &quot;suicide by Nazi.&quot; So double check to make sure he's not armed before throwing your punch. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a Texan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T17:05:46-08:00","id":1039165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1039164#post1039164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a Texan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am too. I've seen first hand that picking fights with people who are armed often does not end well. That's why I suggested that if you are serious about playing at being a hero of justice and going forth to punch people, you should take appropriate precautions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-28-2017, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T23:43:10-08:00","id":1039283,"title":"","content":"If I actually thought that violence would be effective in stopping white supremacy I may be willing to support this punching, but I feel that committing violence on one person who probably won't amount to much. The true IMHO solution would be to utterly deprive them of any form of communication technology or platform that would allow them to spread their ideas and if possible erase their written rhetoric wherever it maybe. Outright criminalizing white supremacy/Nazism ideology would also go a long in helping<br /> <br /> Probably not very feasible and highly illegal in the Land of the Free, but my desire is to ironically enough wipe-out white supremacy from existence and not simply marginalize it and hope it doesn't catch on again in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T02:23:43-08:00","id":1039323,"title":"","content":"As I tried to point out, it's not necessarily about stopping white supremacy, or even impacting the beliefs of the person that got punched. Sometimes it's a message to everyone that's scared that there are people out there that will put themselves on the line to stand up for you. To reassure people that instead of, &quot;First they came for the X, but I did nothing because I was not an X,&quot; we will have, &quot;They came for the X, and then people of moral conviction X and not X alike did whatever was necessary to protect the X.&quot; Even if it does nothing but feed the false persecution complex Neo-Nazi's try to spread, they know that if they don't stick to their little rallies that nobody cares about, they're facing a country that will fight back on whatever field they try to use to oppress others.<br /> <br /> I remember listening to a town hall-ish thing Bernie Sanders did after the election where he sat with four Trump voters (IIRC in Wisconsin) in a district that usually goes Democrat but swung Trump to listen to why these people voted for Trump, and to let other people in the community ask them questions. A Muslim women that was in the audience asked about one of the obvious questions of how they could vote for Trump considering all the stuff he said about people like her. There was some of the annoying &quot;take him seriously, but not literally&quot; garbage, but one of the four said to her that as a patriotic American, he would stand up and fight for her if the government - Trump lead or other - tried to attack her rights.<br /> <br /> But to me, that rings completely hollow. If you can't stand up for other people in the security and safety of a ballot booth, where are you going to find the balls to stand up for people when the FBI rolls in to town to bug all the Mosques? I don't think any minority group that's got a reasonable fear of what the Trump administration is going to mean for their safety has any reason to trust that guy is going to do anything meaningful for them when the chips are down. I'd absolutely believe the guy that punched Richard Spencer would go into a Mosque to remove the immoral surveillance that Trump said he wants done if Muslims don't &quot;turn each other in,&quot; in complete defiance of the law being twisted to allow it (sparing the peaceful worshipers their even more trouble).<br /> <br /> Sure, the USA could use better hate crime laws, and stronger laws for going after hate speech (esp. by dumping the aforementioned Brandenburg test), but even that wouldn't get rid of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T17:18:46-08:00","id":1039699,"title":"","content":"I object strongly to the idea that anyone going around and punching people outside of very specific situations (like defending others from direct physical harm) should be called &quot;a hero of justice&quot;. You are no better than them by doing so or saying that you would do so, ironically enough. This is, by the way, why I have no innate respect for US veterans (I could respect one, but not for being a US veteran - for something they did specifically) and I'm disgusted by the veteran worship in the US.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T19:50:38-08:00","id":1039764,"title":"","content":"You also live in a country where guys like Richard Spencer would be in jail because of multiple counts of abusing his freedom of speech to verbally attack minorities.<br /> <br /> You accept that there are circumstances where punching a bad person is OK. I'm not going to say there's a right answer to this, but: How do you judge that in regards to actions that many countries consider illegal, but is perfectly legal in the US? If our laws deny us a legal avenue to stop emotional and verbal abuse by such people, does that change whether or not physical violence is acceptable by the public against them?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T20:57:48-08:00","id":1039805,"title":"","content":"Double posted for some reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T20:57:48-08:00","id":1039806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1039764#post1039764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You also live in a country where guys like Richard Spencer would be in jail because of multiple counts of abusing his freedom of speech to verbally attack minorities.<br /> <br /> You accept that there are circumstances where punching a bad person is OK. I'm not going to say there's a right answer to this, but: How do you judge that in regards to actions that many countries consider illegal, but is perfectly legal in the US? If our laws deny us a legal avenue to stop emotional and verbal abuse by such people, does that change whether or not physical violence is acceptable by the public against them?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're suggesting that vigilantism is acceptable, and that's an incredibly dangerous thing because once you say that people can take the law into their own hands, then anyone (even people on the &quot;other side&quot;) can make use of that argument to take the law into <i>their</i> hands as well.<br /> <br /> Just to point out, what your saying is incredibly close to popular talking points we've seen from the radical right for years. I mean, let me just slightly reword what you said and this statement could have literally been lifted from a far-right, anti-abortion call to arms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You accept that there are circumstances where punching a bad person is OK. I'm not going to say there's a right answer to this, but: How do you judge that in regards to actions that many countries consider illegal, but is perfectly legal in the US? If our laws deny us a legal avenue to stop ***abortionists from killing babies***, does that change whether or not physical violence is acceptable by the public against them? </div> </div> </div>I mean, abortion is illegal in many countries. And if it's okay to physically attack someone who is merely <i>talking</i> about killing people, then (for those who believe that life begins at conception), surely it must be okay to attack someone who is <i>actually</i> killing people.<br /> <br /> Fortunately for us (and by us I mean other pro-Choice people), the vast majority of the far right flatly reject that kind of thinking. Even if they do believe that abortion is murder, they still feel that the appropriate way to challenge abortion doctors isn't with their fists, but rather to elect politicians who will make abortion illegal. And they have been having a fair amount of success at that over the years, which is worrying but probably not <i>as</i> worrying as if they were going around literally attacking people.<br /> <br /> Likewise, people on the left who want to see hate speech made illegal need to start up a movement to get representatives elected into Congress who will pass a law to outlaw hate speech. Most likely it would come down to an amendment to the Constitution. And if that fails? Try and try again until you convince people that this wrong needs to be righted.<br /> <br /> But you don't get to beat people up because the laws don't work the way you want them to, regardless of what side of the political spectrum you're on, how righteous you feel your cause is, or how horrible you believe the other to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-29-2017, 12:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T01:01:24-08:00","id":1039877,"title":"","content":"I think someone earlier brought up how people critical of punching Nazis seem to not be nearly as loud when state-sponsored violence is the subject. With that in mind, it's particularly distressing that <a href=\"http://www.azcentral.com/story/news/politics/onpolitics/2017/01/29/national-security-council-stephen-bannon-presidential-memo/97210776/\" target=\"_blank\">Trump removed our highest military officer from his place on the National Security Council and gave a spot to Bannon</a>, who has openly and frequently aligned himself with white nationalists. Bannon has definitely emerged as the power behind the throne, and this is particularly distressing given that <a href=\"http://www.reuters.com/article/us-cia-killlist-idUSTRE79475C20111005\" target=\"_blank\">a panel under this council can just decide to kill people.</a><br /> <br /> I'm aware I'm intruding on a debate on a more narrow issue, but I needed to express to <i>someone</i> &quot;Jesus <i>Christ</i>, how horrifying.&quot; The influence Bannon wields is what lead to the refugee ban, and this new spot on the Council makes me worried about further things along this line, like classifying BLM as a domestic terror organization or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T01:10:59-08:00","id":1039880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1039806#post1039806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're suggesting that vigilantism is acceptable, and that's an incredibly dangerous thing because once you say that people can take the law into their own hands, then anyone (even people on the &quot;other side&quot;) can make use of that argument to take the law into <i>their</i> hands as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm suggesting that this isn't actually a simple moral calculus.<br /> <br /> As well, we codify into law a certain amount of &quot;vigilantism&quot; as it is, the law just decides on certain acceptable lines. If I see someone being beaten up, I'm allowed to use force to protect them. If I see someone committing a crime, I have a right to use necessary force to restrain them until proper authorities arrive.<br /> <br /> Since the law is not constructed on a strictly defined ethical method, what counts as &quot;vigilantism&quot; and what's a citizen's right to help enforce the law is at odds with trying to abide by a moral system. Yes, this applies to people that would do things I would not support as well. But I have my personal ethical arguments to keep myself confident in my positions; but I'll acknowledge that this can't force other people to abide by them and behave in what I'd consider an ethically appropriate fashion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just to point out, what your saying is incredibly close to popular talking points we've seen from the radical right for years. </div> </div> </div>Despite my political leanings, this is meaningless to me. The radical right as a whole isn't inherently incapable of making reasoned arguments for their positions even if I disagree with their conclusions. And &quot;incredibly close&quot; in this regard basically means, &quot;there's nuance that matters but I'm ignoring it try to make a point even if that ultimately detracts from my point.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, that whole abortion rhetoric thing isn't really that far right, even if the center-right has moved away from open support of it. And we've seen plenty of non-violent attempts to restrict abortion rights that have been orders of magnitude more successful than all the violence done to try to stop abortion ever could have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, abortion is illegal in many countries. </div> </div> </div>Abortion is only flatly illegal in seven countries in the world (one of which is Vatican City... which is surrounded by Italy which has fully legal abortion rights, making it a meaningless law). The vast majority of countries accept at least some need for legal abortions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And they have been having a fair amount of success at that over the years, which is worrying but probably not <i>as</i> worrying as if they were going around literally attacking people. </div> </div> </div>The only reason why attacks on abortion providers are down, is because of the success in the legal arena that's been going on. While the policy makes on the right were trying to figure out ways to undermine Roe v Wade in application, there was a lot of violence against abortion providers (including outright murders).<br /> <br /> I also have no interest in litigating this specific example. I think we can agree though, that there's an important nuance here: mainstream society all agrees that bigoted motivated violence is wrong without exception; it is never OK to harm another person simply for being of an ethnic background, a religion, etc., mainstream society is conflicted on the morality of abortion.<br /> <br /> I think that difference matters enough to not be worried about the implications you're making about my position.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But you don't get to beat people up because the laws don't work the way you want them to, regardless of what side of the political spectrum you're on, how righteous you feel your cause is, or how horrible you believe the other to be. </div> </div> </div>Well, you don't have a legal defense in court. You get to do it because it's very hard to actually stop people from doing it. The whole concept of civil disobedience is, after all, breaking the law for the sole reason of demonstrating that the law is broken. Civil disobedience can be very effective, and while modern civil disobedience focuses on non-violent forms of it, not all cases are. If there's no moral way to protest the law by breaking the law... that means that the Civil Rights protests had no moral grounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T07:29:37-08:00","id":1039974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1039699#post1039699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I object strongly to the idea that anyone going around and punching people outside of very specific situations (like defending others from direct physical harm) should be called &quot;a hero of justice&quot;. You are no better than them by doing so or saying that you would do so, ironically enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>I object strongly to the idea that wanting to punch one person makes someone just as bad as wanting to commit genocide. That argument requires an extreme degree of moral absolutism when it comes to violence, and I can't get behind that. I think most people would agree that some violence is worse than others, and that punching someone ranks lower than mass murder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T09:59:20-08:00","id":1040064,"title":"","content":"You may want to punch them as much as you want. The moment when you go and start punching without being physically attacked first or reacting to someone being physically attacked (so, self defence or defence), you are just a violent brute. Lesser evil is still evil - you are not a good person because you used violence on a bad person. You still used violence, and justyfing yourself that &quot;it's ok because the guy is a bad person&quot; is exactly the same thing they do - &quot;it's ok because they are bad people from my point of view&quot;.<br /> And yes, if you are wondering, I also strongly oppose death penalty and consider it to be one of greatest failures of any country that employs it. &quot;You killed 100000 people&quot; still isn't a reason for &quot;we are going to murder you in return&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 01-29-2017, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T10:17:10-08:00","id":1040078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040064#post1040064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may want to punch them as much as you want. The moment when you go and start punching without being physically attacked first or reacting to someone being physically attacked (so, self defence or defence), you are just a violent brute.</div> </div> </div> </div>Violent, sure, but not necessarily a brute. There's thoughtfulness to it, an attempt to curb a detrimental culture, rather than close-minded hate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lesser evil is still evil - you are not a good person because you used violence on a bad person. You still used violence, and justyfing yourself that &quot;it's ok because the guy is a bad person&quot; is exactly the same thing they do - &quot;it's ok because they are bad people from my point of view&quot;. </div> </div> </div>That implies that violence is never acceptable. 'It's okay because the guy is a bad person' is not exactly what Nazis do. They use violence because they believe you are subhuman and you and anyone like you deserves to be wiped off the face of the planet. How is using violence against that any different from using violence against someone who is planning to kill you or someone you care about? Is a police officer evil because they shot someone who might have otherwise killed a dozen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T10:34:06-08:00","id":1040085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040064#post1040064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may want to punch them as much as you want. The moment when you go and start punching without being physically attacked first or reacting to someone being physically attacked (so, self defence or defence), you are just a violent brute.</div> </div> </div> </div>And how about acting in defense of others? Spenser may not have physically attacked anyone (that we know of), but he is engaging in violence against groups of people. If you ask me, non-physical violence isn't inherently less serious than physical violence.<br /> <br /> Besides that, the assertion that acting with physical violence in any capacity beyond self-defense against physical violence defines the person as a violent brute is still absolutist to a degree I can't support.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040064#post1040064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lesser evil is still evil - you are not a good person because you used violence on a bad person.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this 100%. However, I would counter that you're not a bad person because of it either. People are more nuanced than that. I am more inclined towards the perspective that the good a person has done does not erase the bad they have done, nor the bad the good, than the one that says if half an onion is rotten then it's a rotten onion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040064#post1040064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You still used violence, and justyfing yourself that &amp;quot;it's ok because the guy is a bad person&amp;quot; is exactly the same thing they do - &amp;quot;it's ok because they are bad people from my point of view&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how I justify it. I find it distasteful to define people as good people and bad people. Rather, people's actions are what should be assessed. The reasoning people like Spenser use to justify the murder of entire ethnic groups is &quot;they're bad people because of their genetics.&quot; The reasoning I use to justify punching Spenser and people like him is &quot;he is engaging in non-physical violence against entire ethnic groups and advocating for their extermination.&quot; To treat those justifications as equivalent is frankly ridiculous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040064#post1040064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, if you are wondering, I also strongly oppose death penalty and consider it to be one of greatest failures of any country that employs it. &amp;quot;You killed 100000 people&amp;quot; still isn't a reason for &amp;quot;we are going to murder you in return&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. But this discussion isn't about the death penalty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T10:42:19-08:00","id":1040087,"title":"","content":"If they shot someone without being in direct danger of being harmed themselves, or without it being in order to directly save someone right there right now? Then yes, shooting the guy on the spot with an excuse of &quot;he was a monster&quot; doesn't make you a hero. <br /> Again, I'm not condemning anyone for punching someone when they are directly defending themselves from being physically harmed. I object to idealizing vigilantism, and I object to the mindset that violence is noble simply because you are using it against someone you dislike, even if you have legitimate reasons for the dislike. If, after hearing that someone broke my mothers ribs in multiple places, I would go and find that person and brutalize them, I would be no better than them. Same thing for people who used violence against me. <br /> Then again, I'm speaking from a country where indeed being a nazi, a communist or anything else that's built on group-targeted hatred is simply illegal. I'm kinda shocked that, from what I can read here, these groups have much more freedom to organize or even maybe act under US law. What is the context of that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T11:06:47-08:00","id":1040097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040087#post1040087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they shot someone without being in direct danger of being harmed themselves, or without it being in order to directly save someone right there right now? Then yes, shooting the guy on the spot with an excuse of &quot;he was a monster&quot; doesn't make you a hero.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can we stop that? Heavy Arms didn't say he was being a hero or heroic, and associating it with his reasoning seems like it's trying to belittle his reasons for some desire for grandeur.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, I'm not condemning anyone for punching someone when they are directly defending themselves from being physically harmed. I object to idealizing vigilantism, and I object to the mindset that violence is noble simply because you are using it against someone you dislike, even if you have legitimate reasons for the dislike. If, after hearing that someone broke my mothers ribs in multiple places, I would go and find that person and brutalize them, I would be no better than them. Same thing for people who used violence against me. </div> </div> </div>This is the crux of the problem, as stated. If someone uses violence against you in an attempt to kill, you have to be fast or dead. 'It's only okay to use violence in self defense,' means you cannot be proactive against people that will be. Even some self-defense laws work against the perceived threat of danger, not just the imminent presence of it. What you're describing is vengeance. A more accurate example situation would be if someone lived next to your mother and announced online and in public that they thought your mother was detrimental to humanity and that they believe the world would be better off if she was gone from it. They have an online community to support laws to get rid of your mother and hinder her ability to do things, they actively recruit from the aforementioned 'proactive' violent people and glorify violence against people like your mother, without actually saying they're going to hurt your mother, and the rhetoric is escalating. There's whole subreddits about it, there's rallies and marches outside of your mom's house. And you kill the man to end it, because you know sooner or later someone is likely to try killing your mom to end it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then again, I'm speaking from a country where indeed being a nazi, a communist or anything else that's built on group-targeted hatred is simply illegal. I'm kinda shocked that, from what I can read here, these groups have much more freedom to organize or even maybe act under US law. What is the context of that? </div> </div> </div>Freedom of speech, freedom to organize, that kind of thing. We make exceptions for it with some things, but fascism and racism are hard to abolish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T12:11:23-08:00","id":1040130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040087#post1040087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, I'm not condemning anyone for punching someone when they are directly defending themselves from being physically harmed. I object to idealizing vigilantism, and I object to the mindset that violence is noble simply because you are using it against someone you dislike, even if you have legitimate reasons for the dislike.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I think this may be the root of our disagreement. Maybe I'm not expressing myself clearly enough, because I am not of the mindset that violence is ever noble, nor that it is excused simply because the perpetrator dislikes the victim. I am of the opinion that when someone poses a danger to other people, violence can be an appropriate reponse. It is not a preferred response, and should be a last resort, but there are times when violence is the only way to prevent other people (and/or yourself) from getting hurt. And I am not of the opinion that the danger posed necessarily has to be immediately imminent. If someone threatens to murder you, you don't wait for them to prove they have a weapon. You take immediate action. Maybe you call the police rather than engaging them in physical conflict, but you sure as hell don't shrug and tell yourself he has the right to say that as long as he's not currently in the process of trying to murder you. If someone earnestly says things like &quot;we need to ask ourselves if the world needs the black race&quot;, speaks at neo-nazi rallies, and gets crowds of people chanting &quot;hail trump&quot;, you don't wait for them to get enough support that they actually start murdering people. But if you live in America, that's all perfectly legal. Promote violence against whatever group you want, as long as you aren't directly engaging in the violence yourself, and you're not posing threat of immediate violence, the law can't touch you. Not only that, you're protected under the law from anyone who tries to stop you from doing it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040087#post1040087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then again, I'm speaking from a country where indeed being a nazi, a communist or anything else that's built on group-targeted hatred is simply illegal. I'm kinda shocked that, from what I can read here, these groups have much more freedom to organize or even maybe act under US law. What is the context of that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Until speech poses immediate danger of inciting illegal activity, it's protected under the first amendment. So you can't call the cops like you would with the guy who threatened to murder you. All you can legally do is wait for them to start walking their talk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T12:29:32-08:00","id":1040137,"title":"","content":"One of my problems with how you're going about this WHW, is the unstated reasoning behind by physical violence is a special kind of violence.<br /> <br /> Why is it only OK to use physical violence to prevent physical violence? Why is using physical violence to prevent emotional violence wrong?<br /> <br /> If three men are standing over a boy, and berating him relentlessly, throwing insult after insult, saying the most offensive things you can imagine, and the boy is laying there crying and sobbing. You try to get them to stop with words, and they only ignore you. They don't seem to have any intent to touch the boy.<br /> <br /> Do you let this continue until the police arrive? Or do you use force to stop it? Are you a &quot;brutish thug&quot; for pulling these men away and even punching one of them? Or are you a moral person for defending this boy? Are you a vigilante, or a good citizen standing up for the rights of the others?<br /> <br /> We can argue about the specifics of what happened with Richard Spencer and all that, but the more general philosophic point here needs to be addressed. Is physical violence ever acceptable against non-physical violence?<br /> <br /> At the moment, you seem to be arguing that nobody should help this boy. That they should just wait for the police. That the boy has to endure both the verbal assault, and the knowledge that everyone else is just going to stand there and watch his trauma because none of them will stop it as long as it's just words, because hurting these men would be worse.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040087#post1040087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then again, I'm speaking from a country where indeed being a nazi, a communist or anything else that's built on group-targeted hatred is simply illegal. I'm kinda shocked that, from what I can read here, these groups have much more freedom to organize or even maybe act under US law. What is the context of that?</div> </div> </div> </div>We've mentioned something called the Brandenburg test. This was a ruling by our Supreme Court that stated that incitement to harm (so using speech to encourage other people to do bad things) is only illegal if a reasonable person would feel the phrasing is asking for immediate action.<br /> <br /> This grants hate groups an obscene about of leeway to speak without consequence, and insulate leaders from the actions of followers.<br /> <br /> So, a Nazi leader can say, &quot;Jews are an abomination, and in a perfect world they would all be killed for their horrible ways, and all their unholy gathering places would be burnt down.&quot; And even if their followers go and burn down a synagogue, the leader is safe from the law. The leader didn't say, &quot;go burn down a synagogue,&quot; or, &quot;and we need to start doing this now.&quot; There is no law to punish him for spreading these teachings with, even if we know those that listen will then go out and act on them.<br /> <br /> That is the level of freedom we grant hate groups here. We deny ourselves the ability to punish the leaders of hate groups (such as Richard Spencer), and can only do anything about the followers that act on those teachings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T12:34:31-08:00","id":1040144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1038985#post1038985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok. Let's talk about some nonviolent approaches to option B.<br /> <br /> 1. Deprive the target of money by turning their customers/clients/investors off them.<br /> 2. Deprive the target of social influence by damaging their reputation, connections, venues, or partners.<br /> 3. Directly attack the target through the legal system by suing them or by inviting suits from them that they cannot win.<br /> 4. Deprive the target of power by forcing adjustments to whatever policies/laws/regulations they are exploiting.<br /> \u200b5. Do any of the above to people close to the target - friends, family, allies in the community.<br /> <br /> If you're determined that you've got to punish someone to deter them or neutralize them, there's a lot of ways to mess people up without ever laying a hand on them. Words are almost as deadly as guns, if you say them in the right way at the right time to the right person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Missed this.<br /> <br /> 1) This presumes I have anything resembling the power to actually do that in a way that doesn't involve gross violence and property damage.<br /> 2) This presumes I have anything resembling the power to actually do that in a way that doesn't involve crass public displays.<br /> 3) This presumes I have anything resembling the power to actually do that in any way period.<br /> 4) This presumes I have anything resembling the power to actually do that in any way that does not involve violent revolution.<br /> 5) This presumes all of the above and also shifts the punishment to other people. If those people are worth acting against, sure, but if not, keep the fight to the ones fighting.<br /> <br /> Words are powerful when delivered by people in positions of power. I'm a relative nobody on the internet.<br /> <br /> Also, words don't stop assholes from grabbing Muslim women's heads and ripping off their burkas. Words don't stop a gang of white supremacists from following a black kid and verbally tearing him apart. Words don't stop the queerbashers from literally bashing queers. Words might temporarily push them back, but it does not set the precedent-&quot;Do this and people will fight you.&quot;<br /> <br /> Words are great for systems on the long haul and people open to change, but in the meantime, physical action is an essential part of fighting the clear and present harm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-29-2017, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T12:35:55-08:00","id":1040146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1039974#post1039974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I object strongly to the idea that wanting to punch one person makes someone just as bad as wanting to commit genocide. That argument requires an extreme degree of moral absolutism when it comes to violence, and I can't get behind that. I think most people would agree that some violence is worse than others, and that punching someone ranks lower than mass murder.</div> </div> </div> </div>This idea, that talking about genocide is <i>just as bad</i> as actually committing genocide seems completely chilling and alien to me. Like, I'm not trying to be a jerk here but I literally don't understand the thought process. Words are words. Actions are actions. If someone is committing mass murder then yes, you should stop him in any way you can and punching that person is absolutely the lesser of the two evils. But if someone is merely discussing genocide, it's just that, words and punching someone is worse. This idea that we should treat people who are discussing or calling for a given act as if they were actively engaging in that act is just something I can't wrap my mind around. That just seems so contrary to basic western principles.<br /> <br /> I mean, should someone who talks about killing another person be treated as if they were in fact committing murder? Should members of NAMBLA, which push for methods by which pedophilia should be legalized, be treated as if they were actively engaging in pedophilia? Should people be able to go up and punch radical Muslims who support globalist jihad, even if they have never actually done anything beyond agree with the philosophy of a group like ISIS or Al-Queda?<br /> <br /> Or to put it another way, do you feel that mass murder is unique in that it is the <i>only</i> subject about which if someone discusses it, physical violence is an acceptable response? If so, why? And if not, what other subjects that people write about or talk about would you consider violence a reasonable response to? Is it okay to attack anyone who decides to say or write things that are viewed as hateful and socially unacceptable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T12:35:59-08:00","id":1040147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040097#post1040097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can we stop that? Heavy Arms didn't say he was being a hero or heroic, and associating it with his reasoning seems like it's trying to belittle his reasons for some desire for grandeur.</div> </div> </div> </div>In fairness, I think is an argument made about me and others like me while said to Arms. I do have a shadow on this conversation.<br /> <br /> (Or I might be aggrandizing my own importance, one of the two)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T12:42:12-08:00","id":1040152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040097#post1040097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the crux of the problem, as stated. If someone uses violence against you in an attempt to kill, you have to be fast or dead. 'It's only okay to use violence in self defense,' means you cannot be proactive against people that will be. Even some self-defense laws work against the perceived threat of danger, not just the imminent presence of it. What you're describing is vengeance. A more accurate example situation would be if someone lived next to your mother and announced online and in public that they thought your mother was detrimental to humanity and that they believe the world would be better off if she was gone from it. They have an online community to support laws to get rid of your mother and hinder her ability to do things, they actively recruit from the aforementioned 'proactive' violent people and glorify violence against people like your mother, without actually saying they're going to hurt your mother, and the rhetoric is escalating. There's whole subreddits about it, there's rallies and marches outside of your mom's house. And you kill the man to end it, because you know sooner or later someone is likely to try killing your mom to end it.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a nutshell, this was the George W. Bush administration's argument for Preemptive War. That, if you have a really, really, good idea that someone else is going to attack or hurt you, you have the right to go attack him before he can attack you.<br /> <br /> It just seems so weird to hear essentially the same argument coming from liberals a decade and a half later - that when you believe someone is going to attack you, it's okay to preemptively attack that person before they have a chance to hurt you.<br /> <br /> Seriously, sometimes I feel like I fell into Bizarro World where conservatives and liberal suddenly decided to exchange their values.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T12:59:41-08:00","id":1040160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040147#post1040147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fairness, I think is an argument made about me and others like me while said to Arms. I do have a shadow on this conversation.<br /> <br /> (Or I might be aggrandizing my own importance, one of the two)</div> </div> </div> </div>Your comments did seem more pro-vigilantism, but you weren't declaring yourself a 'hero of justice' because you believed sometimes you were doing what was right. And it did seem to be shifting to Heavy Arms.<br /> <br /> Interesting thread, hard to dance around the rules. Morally, there's clearly some different stances here, both are understandable. The disagreement seems to hinge upon the threat of Nazism and whether it is just free speech or if it is speech that to nothing but violence.<br /> <br /> Then, legally, we're discussing about illegal activities in response to potential illegal activities, or to halt the warping of laws to unjust terms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040152#post1040152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a nutshell, this was the George W. Bush administration's argument for Preemptive War. That, if you have a really, really, good idea that someone else is going to attack or hurt you, you have the right to go attack him before he can attack you.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair there was more than that argument for it. Weapons of Mass Destruction was the easy sale, but the human rights abuses and overall 'War on Terror' were part of the argument.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It just seems so weird to hear essentially the same argument coming from liberals a decade and a half later - that when you believe someone is going to attack you, it's okay to preemptively attack that person before they have a chance to hurt you. </div> </div> </div>It's not exactly the same argument. A nation has its own laws, while a Nazi next door is supposed to be living under the same laws as yourself. And there's agency. If you punch a Nazi, thats your choice, as is your choice to suffer potential consequences for it. If your leader drags your entire country into war, that's not your choice but is suddenly your burden. The price paid is not one going to be felt by them. And war brings chaos and destruction with it, civilians are hurt and killed, punching a Nazi has its own repercussions but isn't bringing the 'mass destruction' to the party.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Seriously, sometimes I feel like I fell into Bizarro World where conservatives and liberal suddenly decided to exchange their values. </div> </div> </div>It helps if you remember that everything is not black and white and groups aren't hive minds, liberals are not all hippie peaceniks and all conservatives are not nazis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-29-2017, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T13:33:04-08:00","id":1040178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040146#post1040146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This idea, that talking about genocide is <i>just as bad</i> as actually committing genocide seems completely chilling and alien to me. Like, I'm not trying to be a jerk here but I literally don't understand the thought process. Words are words. Actions are actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think talking about genocide is as bad as actually committing genocide, The comment you qoted was in response to WHW saying that if you <i>want</i> to punch someone for it, you're as bad as they are. I do believe that wanting to commit genocide is worse than wanting to punch someone who wants to commit genocide. I also don't think punching people is good, but I do believe there are some situations where there is no good option, and I believe this is one of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040146#post1040146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If someone is committing mass murder then yes, you should stop him in any way you can and punching that person is absolutely the lesser of the two evils. But if someone is merely discussing genocide, it's just that, words and punching someone is worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>So we shouldn't do anything about people who are seriously considering genocide until after they've started killing people?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040146#post1040146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This idea that we should treat people who are discussing or calling for a given act as if they were actively engaging in that act is just something I can't wrap my mind around. That just seems so contrary to basic western principles.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fine, it's not an idea I hold.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040146#post1040146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, should someone who talks about killing another person be treated as if they were in fact committing murder?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but if they are making plans to commit murder, we shouldn't wait for them to actually do it before trying to stop them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040146#post1040146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should members of NAMBLA, which push for methods by which pedophilia should be legalized, be treated as if they were actively engaging in pedophilia?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not, but we shouldn't wait for a child to get molested before doing anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040146#post1040146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should people be able to go up and punch radical Muslims who support globalist jihad, even if they have never actually done anything beyond agree with the philosophy of a group like ISIS or Al-Queda?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean. If they're actually advocating for others to engage in acts of terrorism? I'm not going to be too upset if someone punches them, no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040146#post1040146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or to put it another way, do you feel that mass murder is unique in that it is the <i>only</i> subject about which if someone discusses it, physical violence is an acceptable response? If so, why? And if not, what other subjects that people write about or talk about would you consider violence a reasonable response to? Is it okay to attack anyone who decides to say or write things that are viewed as hateful and socially unacceptable?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I really don't think violence should have to be the response to people organizing to advocate for the committing of large-scale atrocities. But the way our laws are framed, nothing can be done about it legally until it's decided that the threat is immediate. I don't think we should be so permissive of speech that promotes illegal activity simply because it promotes it in the long term. Since that is not the case, however, I'm not going to be upset when someone gives the people doing the advocacy an &quot;alternative fist bump.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-29-2017, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T13:56:13-08:00","id":1040198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040178#post1040178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So we shouldn't do anything about people who are seriously considering genocide until after they've started killing people?</div> </div> </div> </div>The law shouldn't be able to do anything to anyone until they they start taking concrete, physical steps to begin killing people and move beyond words and philosophy and into actual actions, the same as for any other potential would-be-criminal. I don't want to see the police arresting people just because they <i>believe</i> someone is going to commit a crime at some point down the road or just because someone <i>says</i> they would like to commit a crime. <br /> <br /> Even when dealing with threats on the life of the president (one of the more serious things you can say), the Secret Service will investigate, but they can't throw someone in jail or punish them under the law, unless there is evidence that the person was planning to take actual, physical steps to assassinate the president.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040178#post1040178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I really don't think violence should have to be the response to people organizing to advocate for the committing of large-scale atrocities. But the way our laws are framed, nothing can be done about it legally until it's decided that the threat is immediate. I don't think we should be so permissive of speech that promotes illegal activity simply because it promotes it in the long term. Since that is not the case, however, I'm not going to be upset when someone gives the people doing the advocacy an &quot;alternative fist bump.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>So in the meantime then, it's perfectly acceptable to use physical violence today, against someone who says they would like to commit a crime at some vague, undefined point in the future, which they may or may not ever get around to actually committing?<br /> <br /> Again, if you're unhappy with the fact that the law lets people say things you find grossly offensive, then you should be protesting to change the law to silence those people, not using physical assaults to intimidate those people into silence. Anyone who does use physical violence to intimidate someone into silence is simply a thug, even if the person they're silencing is human filth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-29-2017, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T14:13:28-08:00","id":1040209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040160#post1040160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It helps if you remember that everything is not black and white and groups aren't hive minds, liberals are not all hippie peaceniks and all conservatives are not nazis.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true, but I mentioned in another thread a couple of months ago, about how I feel like the left is moving very far away from where it was when I was growing up. Twenty-five years ago if someone asked, &quot;Is it okay to punch a dude because of the things he says?&quot; there would have been a resounding, &quot;NO!&quot; from the Left. Now you're getting a heck of a lot of people saying, &quot;Absolutely!&quot;<br /> <br /> Violence is becoming more acceptable and mainstream, and I find that worrying, especially coming from the left which has traditionally chosen to focus on non-violent protests and movements rather than in going around to physically attack people. The danger is, of course, when people on the left start using violence and justifying it by saying, &quot;The laws let this guy get away with something I think should be illegal,&quot; it's only a matter of time before other people start doing the same.<br /> <br /> And while I have no personal objection to punching white supremacists, some of the other groups that will inevitably start using the same logical to justify why it's acceptable to use physical violence against people who say (or do) things they feel should be illegal, make me quite worried at the potential problems down the road.<br /> <br /> Violence is one of those things that's really hard to put back in the bag once you start using it - if it's an option for you, it becomes an option for other people as well. And do you really want those other guys feeling that they should be able to physically attack people because the law doesn't work the way they want it to?<br /> <br /> Well, this is why I like discussing things on the forum, lots of people have views that are much different from mine, but sometimes I do find myself feeling a bit old and trying to figure out where things have gone since I was younger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T14:48:20-08:00","id":1040219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040198#post1040198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The law shouldn't be able to do anything to anyone until they they start taking concrete, physical steps to begin killing people and move beyond words and philosophy and into actual actions, the same as for any other potential would-be-criminal. I don't want to see the police arresting people just because they <i>believe</i> someone is going to commit a crime at some point down the road or just because someone <i>says</i> they would like to commit a crime.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't someone saying they want to commit a crime, this is someone actively encouraging others to commit crime on a massive scale. Spenser is smart enough to know that the law is on his side as long as he doesn't directly participate in illegal activity. All he has to do is stoke the flames of people dumb enough to do what he says.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040146#post1040146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in the meantime then, it's perfectly acceptable to use physical violence today, against someone who says they would like to commit a crime at some vague, undefined point in the future, which they may or may not ever get around to actually committing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfectly acceptable? No. But it is all some people can do in the face of a very real threat to the safety of millions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040146#post1040146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, if you're unhappy with the fact that the law lets people say things you find grossly offensive, then you should be protesting to change the law to silence those people, not using physical assaults to intimidate those people into silence.</div> </div> </div> </div>The former is what I am doing (though honestly the chances of a SCOTUS decision being overturned by later Justices is pretty low - they know that's a dangerous game to play). But I'm not condemning the latter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040146#post1040146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone who does use physical violence to intimidate someone into silence is simply a thug, even if the person they're silencing is human filth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just can't classify people as &quot;thugs&quot; and &quot;human filth&quot;. I assess <i>actions</i>, and the act of advocating in favor of global atrocities is one I don't believe should be protected. The law protects them, and I don't plan to break it, but I won't fault people for breaking a law I see as unjust.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T14:53:07-08:00","id":1040225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040146#post1040146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Words are words. Actions are actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have an honest question:<br /> <br /> To what level are people responsible for the effects of their words?<br /> <br /> Because that's half of the debate about this (The other half is the application of violence).<br /> <br /> I'm a raging liberal feminist, but from my perspective the left/right division on the issue looks like this:<br /> <br /> The left hold that people are accountable for the impact their words have on other people, which is why they buzz angrily when people start dropping slurs or hate speech. It's why the left has pushed towards pointing out problematic trends in media and attempting to discourage hateful or toxic words or philosophies from spreading.<br /> <br /> So from there it makes sense to go, &quot;Advocating genocide is obviously harmful because it (propagates an atmosphere of hostility towards an already maligned minority group/shows radical groups that would act violently against that minority group that their views are socially acceptable/etc).&quot;<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the right seems to state that words have no actual impact on the world, and therefore holding someone accountable for what they say is absurd and stifling. This is why it has kicked backed against what it calls &quot;PC culture&quot;, which it views as a crushing burden on freedom of speech.<br /> <br /> So getting upset at someone advocating genocide would make sense because their words are completely isolated from any action.<br /> <br /> Naturally, I don't agree with the right facing stance, but that should be pretty obvious.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T15:07:53-08:00","id":1040232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040219#post1040219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just can't classify people as &quot;thugs&quot; and &quot;human filth&quot;. I assess <i>actions</i>, and the act of advocating in favor of global atrocities is one I don't believe should be protected. The law protects them, and I don't plan to break it, but I won't fault people for breaking a law I see as unjust.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also classify people based on their actions - people who cover up their face, sucker-punch someone to silence them and then run away so they don't have to face the consequences of their action are thugs. And people who promote global atrocities are human filth.<br /> <br /> But, even if the guy breaking the law and using violence is on &quot;my side&quot; I'll still roundly condemn him for breaking the law and using violence, and I will hope that when people on the other side have their own individuals who choose to use violence to break the laws they feel are unjust, the people on their side roundly condemn them as well.<br /> <br /> Cheering for people who use violence and break the law will only encourage more people to use violence and break the law. As the thread title says, &quot;Violence begets violence.&quot; And while you might not have a problem with someone breaking the laws <i>you</i> see as unjust, the next person using violence to break the law, might use that exact same justification to break laws that you feel <i>are</i> just.<br /> <br /> This sort of philosophical rhetoric, &quot;It's okay to use violence if the laws don't work the way I want them to,&quot; is like a Pandora's Box, because once you open it and allow that you get to use violence if the laws don't function how you like, then other people get to do the same thing. <br /> <br /> And the <i>last</i> thing I want to see is the Left opening up the door to the use of violence and refusing to condemn it when it occurs, because I <i>definitely</i> don't want to see the Right coming to the conclusion that, if the Left believes it's acceptable to engage in violence, then it should be okay for them to do the same thing as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T15:11:10-08:00","id":1040236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040225#post1040225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have an honest question:<br /> <br /> To what level are people responsible for the effects of their words?<br /> <br /> Because that's half of the debate about this (The other half is the application of violence).<br /> <br /> I'm a raging liberal feminist, but from my perspective the left/right division on the issue looks like this:<br /> <br /> The left hold that people are accountable for the impact their words have on other people, which is why they buzz angrily when people start dropping slurs or hate speech. It's why the left has pushed towards pointing out problematic trends in media and attempting to discourage hateful or toxic words or philosophies from spreading.<br /> <br /> So from there it makes sense to go, &amp;quot;Advocating genocide is obviously harmful because it (propagates an atmosphere of hostility towards an already maligned minority group/shows radical groups that would act violently against that minority group that their views are socially acceptable/etc).&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh my god, thank you, this articulates what I've been struggling to express for pages so much more eloquently than I have been able to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040225#post1040225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, the right seems to state that words have no actual impact on the world, and therefore holding someone accountable for what they say is absurd and stifling. This is why it has kicked backed against what it calls &amp;quot;PC culture&amp;quot;, which it views as a crushing burden on freedom of speech.<br /> <br /> So getting upset at someone advocating genocide would make sense because their words are completely isolated from any action.</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who tends to give people the benefit of the doubt as much as I reasonably can, I suspect it comes less from a belief that words have no impact, and more from valuing the freedom to express one's self without restraint, to the point that limiting that ability is seen as outweighing the potential harm caused by the things people say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T15:28:00-08:00","id":1040246,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar741_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"741\" data-vbnamecard=\"741\">AnubisXy</a> I'd like to hear your response to my last hypothetical. About the boy and his harassers.<br /> <br /> Because as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4578_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4578\" data-vbnamecard=\"4578\">Zale</a> has pointed out, you seem to be arguing from a stance were the words people say don't matter; where speaking is not an action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T15:41:37-08:00","id":1040250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040232#post1040232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also classify people based on their actions - people who cover up their face, sucker-punch someone to silence them and then run away so they don't have to face the consequences of their action are thugs. And people who promote global atrocities are human filth.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, no, that's what I <i>don't</i> do. I judge the act, not the actor. Actors are responsible for their actions, but shouldn't be defined by them. That's a whole different debate though, and one that I recognize I hold an extreme view on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040232#post1040232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, even if the guy breaking the law and using violence is on &amp;quot;my side&amp;quot; I'll still roundly condemn him for breaking the law and using violence, and I will hope that when people on the other side have their own individuals who choose to use violence to break the laws they feel are unjust, the people on their side roundly condemn them as well.<br /> <br /> Cheering for people who use violence and break the law will only encourage more people to use violence and break the law. As the thread title says, &amp;quot;Violence begets violence.&amp;quot; And while you might not have a problem with someone breaking the laws <i>you</i> see as unjust, the next person using violence to break the law, might use that exact same justification to break laws that you feel <i>are</i> just.<br /> <br /> This sort of philosophical rhetoric, &amp;quot;It's okay to use violence if the laws don't work the way I want them to,&amp;quot; is like a Pandora's Box, because once you open it and allow that you get to use violence if the laws don't function how you like, then other people get to do the same thing. <br /> <br /> And the <i>last</i> thing I want to see is the Left opening up the door to the use of violence and refusing to condemn it when it occurs, because I <i>definitely</i> don't want to see the Right coming to the conclusion that, if the Left believes it's acceptable to engage in violence, then it should be okay for them to do the same thing as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, the right already opened that box a long time ago. The left has tried ignoring it and it still hasn't closed itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T15:52:57-08:00","id":1040256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040250#post1040250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, the right already opened that box a long time ago. The left has tried ignoring it and it still hasn't closed itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the response is to do the same thing? Like the thread title says, violence begets violence. Unfortunately the only result of that will be to see more and more politically inspired violence on all sides. I guess if that's what you want to see in America, fine, but I know I sure don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T16:15:42-08:00","id":1040268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040246#post1040246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar741_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"741\" data-vbnamecard=\"741\">AnubisXy</a> I'd like to hear your response to my last hypothetical. About the boy and his harassers.<br /> <br /> Because as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4578_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4578\" data-vbnamecard=\"4578\">Zale</a> has pointed out, you seem to be arguing from a stance were the words people say don't matter; where speaking is not an action.</div> </div> </div> </div>You were replying to someone else, but sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040137#post1040137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We can argue about the specifics of what happened with Richard Spencer and all that, but the more general philosophic point here needs to be addressed. Is physical violence ever acceptable against non-physical violence?<br /> <br /> At the moment, you seem to be arguing that nobody should help this boy. That they should just wait for the police. That the boy has to endure both the verbal assault, and the knowledge that everyone else is just going to stand there and watch his trauma because none of them will stop it as long as it's just words, because hurting these men would be worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are certainly specific times in which words move beyond mere words and into demonstrable actions (the classic screaming &quot;FIRE!&quot; in a crowded movie theater for example). Other words can be illegal, like extorting someone by telling them you'll break their legs if they don't give you money, even if the person doesn't actually commit the act of violence.<br /> <br /> So to be clear, words are not <i>always</i> just words, and context does absolutely matter. We do have restrictions on speech in America, even if those restrictions aren't as tight as what you might find in other countries.<br /> <br /> As to your example specifically, I feel it squarely falls under child abuse, which is certainly against the law to my knowledge.<br /> <br /> So I would say that yes, once you've engaged with them and they continue to abuse a child who has no way of leaving or protecting himself, then violence would be a reasonable response to that. You would likely also be arrested and detained by the police for what you did, but if you got everything on camera it's likely they won't give you more than a slap on the wrist.<br /> <br /> *EDIT* But okay, let's say you live in a country where screaming at a kid like in your example isn't considered wrong and anyone can do it legally. Would it still be okay to use violence against the people screaming at the kid? I would say, yes. Leveling that kind of abuse against a child is pretty clearly wrong, and I feel that it's okay to step over the line and use violence in order to protect the kid from immediate harm.<br /> <br /> Likewise, if you lived in a country where it was legal to scream fire in a crowded theater, I don't think it would be immoral to use violence to stop someone from doing that if you believed that their words posed a clear, present and immediate danger to other people around you.<br /> <br /> And that is the key - <b>immediate.</b> I don't feel you should be able to punch that guy in the face today because you believe that, maybe in a few years down the road he's going to scream fire in a theater or detain and yell at a little kid two months from now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-29-2017, 08:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T17:59:01-08:00","id":1040325,"title":"","content":"OK, now please elaborate on what you consider the limits of immediacy.<br /> <br /> Holding to immediacy has issues, was has already been discussed with the Brandenburg test. How soon is soon enough? 1 minutes? 10 minutes? An hour? A day? Etc. How to you construct an ethical standard that reliably tells you how long is too long to not be immediate as long as the perceived threat of harm to yourself or others is reasonable?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T18:45:25-08:00","id":1040349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040325#post1040325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, now please elaborate on what you consider the limits of immediacy.<br /> <br /> Holding to immediacy has issues, was has already been discussed with the Brandenburg test. How soon is soon enough? 1 minutes? 10 minutes? An hour? A day? Etc. How to you construct an ethical standard that reliably tells you how long is too long to not be immediate as long as the perceived threat of harm to yourself or others is reasonable?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not a fan of the Brandenburg test for several reasons and I think it has some problems. But the key word is &quot;imminent,&quot; which I generally do agree with.<br /> <br /> So that means using violence at the specific time the event in question is taking place would be acceptable or if you specifically know that someone is going to go commit criminal activity in the very near future <i>such that the police (or other such institution) would not be able to intervene in time</i> - &quot;Hey, I'm gonna walk down to the end of the street and shoot up my neighbors house.&quot; You could certainly use violence to try and stop that person since waiting for the police would be unacceptable (by the time they got there, the event would be over).<br /> <br /> But if he said, &quot;Hey, next week I'm going to go shoot up my neighbor's house,&quot; you should call the police.<br /> <br /> The alternative would be to suggest that it's ethically okay to attack someone if you believe that they <i>might</i> pose a threat to you (or someone else) at some vague, unspecific time in the future. I assume you would agree that's not acceptable, right?<br /> <br /> Further, I think it's clear Richard Spencer was not planning to actively carry out genocide that day, and was not actively engaged in committing genocide (nor did he pose an immediate threat to anyone's life or physical health) at the time he was attacked. If the person who attacked Spencer had some evidence that Spencer was preparing to go kill people in the very near future, he had plenty of time to go inform the police of it instead of sucker-punching him and then skedaddling.<br /> <br /> So unlike your example of the people screaming at the child, Richard Spencer was not screaming profanities at a child. He also wasn't not engaging in genocide, mass murder or any other criminal behavior at the time he got clobbered (I don't even believe he was talking about genocide when he was attacked, but then I only caught the video the one time on the news).<br /> <br /> Violence is acceptable when it would take too long for the police (or other authorities) to arrive, and therefore you have to take matters into your own hand to protect yourself or someone else from the harm that would occur before the police arrived.<br /> <br /> But if there is is plenty of time to call the police, and there is plenty of time for them to arrive before anything happens, then that's what you should do - not start throwing punches. Does that answer your question?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-29-2017, 09:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T19:11:13-08:00","id":1040368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040064#post1040064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lesser evil is still evil - you are not a good person because you used violence on a bad person.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fine with that. &quot;Good&quot; and &quot;bad&quot; are not things you are; you can only be good or bad in relation to another being. In this case, I can be good to every human being who is not white, Christian, straight, and cisgender, or I can be good to a person who says all those people should be burned to death in ovens. There's no splitting the difference on this one, so, yeah, it's an easy choice for me. I'm gonna suckerpunch a Nazi.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T19:12:44-08:00","id":1040371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1038655#post1038655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now we have liberals advocating punching white supremacists in the face and basically using that same argument. I can't help but chuckle at the irony of that.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I mean realistically, that's just how it is.<br /> <br /> Simply because you can legally say (almost) anything you want doesn't mean there won't be consequences for what you say, and sometimes those consequences could be in the form of fists or even bullets. Obviously anybody using violence on someone because of what they said is committing a crime, and I suppose you can take comfort in the fact that the law will be on your side - you can have the attacker arrested. But that's still a small comfort to anyone who is intimidated into keeping their mouth shut through the threat of physical violence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Physically fighting nazis is nothing new. Jack Kirby, called &quot;the King&quot; for a damn good reason, often said his only politics as a young man was beating the stuffing out of people who supported Hitler.<br /> <br /> The Nazis correctly identified unlimited free speech as the weak spot of liberal democracy. It allowed them to build their forces via protected speech until they were strong enough to act. I do believe in the principle of free speech, but I have no problem throwing the gauntlet down at genocide advocates, which Richard Spencer and his supporters are without question.<br /> <br /> The only reason skinheads were stopped from taking over the streets of several US cities back in the 90s was because the punk movement pushed back at their own internal infestation and physically forced the racists (with help from groups like SHARP) out of Portland Or and a few other cities.<br /> <br /> There's a good reason that one of Gandhi's most disdained quotes are where he said the Jews should have peacefully gone to their deaths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T20:27:05-08:00","id":1040389,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=AnubisXy;n1040349]So that means using violence at the specific time the event in question is taking place would be acceptable or if you specifically know that someone is going to go commit criminal activity in the very near future <i>such that the police (or other such institution) would not be able to intervene in time</i> - &quot;Hey, I'm gonna walk down to the end of the street and shoot up my neighbors house.&quot; You could certainly use violence to try and stop that person since waiting for the police would be unacceptable (by the time they got there, the event would be over).[/quote<br /> <br /> But you're going back to the assumption that the only issue at hand is preventing physical violence. Emotional abuse and verbal violence do not come with clean lines like, &quot;I'm going to shoot someone.&quot;<br /> <br /> Immediacy is simpler with physical violence in some sense, because it involves a distinct act. If you observe a spouse gaslighting their partner, where's the line of when it's acceptable to step in to get the victim out of a solely verbally abusive relationship? Esp. if you live in a place that doesn't give the police a lot of tools to deal with this sort of domestic crime.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Further, I think it's clear Richard Spencer was not planning to actively carry out genocide that day, and was not actively engaged in committing genocide (nor did he pose an immediate threat to anyone's life or physical health) at the time he was attacked. If the person who attacked Spencer had some evidence that Spencer was preparing to go kill people in the very near future, he had plenty of time to go inform the police of it instead of sucker-punching him and then skedaddling. </div> </div> </div>I think Richard Spencer is a clear and obvious risk of public abusive statements to the emotional health of his fellow citizens. He frequently speaks in public with words that only have the purpose of causing emotional trauma in people he doesn't like.<br /> <br /> So, again, we've established that harm/abuse/etc. does not require physical violence, and that physical violence is not off the table for protecting people from non-physical violence. How does your analysis of Spencer rank in that regard, rather than the genocide thing I didn't even bring up?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So unlike your example of the people screaming at the child, Richard Spencer was not screaming profanities at a child. </div> </div> </div>In that moment. He frequently engages in emotionally abuse language in public, esp. to demean people politically and ideologically opposed to them. He's established a pattern of behavior that says he will abuse his rights to speech to verbally abuse others (however slick he is when it comes to dancing the lines of the law).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Violence is acceptable when it would take too long for the police (or other authorities) to arrive, and therefore you have to take matters into your own hand to protect yourself or someone else from the harm that would occur before the police arrived. </div> </div> </div>And what about situations where the law stops the police from intervening?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T20:48:35-08:00","id":1040394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040389#post1040389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Richard Spencer is a clear and obvious risk of public abusive statements to the emotional health of his fellow citizens. He frequently speaks in public with words that only have the purpose of causing emotional trauma in people he doesn't like.<br /> <br /> So, again, we've established that harm/abuse/etc. does not require physical violence, and that physical violence is not off the table for protecting people from non-physical violence. How does your analysis of Spencer rank in that regard, rather than the genocide thing I didn't even bring up?</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is, unlike your example of adults screaming at children, anyone who didn't like what Richard Spencer was saying had the option to simply walk away. If they find what he says to be mentally traumatizing, they can go somewhere else. He can't force anyone to listen to him speak (if he tries that, that's called false imprisonment and is a crime).<br /> <br /> If Richard Spencer was standing there screaming at a child who had nowhere to go (as with what happened to you on the bus in your story earlier) then punching him might be acceptable. But that wasn't the venue and that's not what happened. He was out on the street answering a few questions from a news reporter when someone popped him.<br /> <br /> To ask you a question, if someone is doing something you feel is traumatic to the well-being of other people (but it isn't illegal), do you think it's okay to go over and attack that person if you see them say, walking down the street to drop off their mail?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T21:18:43-08:00","id":1040403,"title":"","content":"You do not have the option of &quot;just walking away&quot; while Nazis are building support and power. If you wait until they have the forces they need to take action, you are waiting until it is too late. This is not about anyone being offended by speech, this is about stopping genocide. Any &quot;that can't happen here&quot; rhetoric requires we ignore the ascent of the &quot;Alt-Right's&quot; self-identified voice to the National Security Council while the Chairman of the Joint Chiefs has been pushed out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T21:31:55-08:00","id":1040412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040394#post1040394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...anyone who didn't like what Richard Spencer was saying had the option to simply walk away.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... if the victim has a chance to escape, you shouldn't help them? If I see a man being physically assaulted, but he's in a situation where he could run away, I shouldn't help him? Seems to be a fairly questionable standard. &quot;Don't help if the victim can get away.&quot;<br /> <br /> Richard Spencer (and many of his ilk) like showing up to counter-&quot;protest&quot; and disrupt others by spewing their hate speech. So Spencer should be able to shut down other people's gatherings by forcing them to either endure his hate, or walk away? I'm not seeing the compelling moral stance here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He was out on the street answering a few questions from a news reporter when someone popped him. </div> </div> </div>If the reports that he was actually punched twice are true (haven't seen a reputable news source attest it yet), is the second punch his fault for not walking away when he hand the chance? Nobody forced him to stick around people that clearly wanted to punch him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To ask you a question, if someone is doing something you feel is traumatic to the well-being of other people (but it isn't illegal), do you think it's okay to go over and attack that person if you see them say, walking down the street to drop off their mail? </div> </div> </div>Is he doing it while dropping off his mail (I ask because that's sort of how you phrased it, and I don't think that's the thrust of your question)?<br /> <br /> Assuming you mean, do I think it would be right to punch Spencer while he was minding his own business on the street (and assuming he's not wearing racist pins/etc. as he pretty much constantly does)? Probably not. Would I think there's a moral case for, say, disrupting one of his interviews so he doesn't get yet another public platform for his hate speech? Absolutely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T21:56:37-08:00","id":1040421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040412#post1040412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... if the victim has a chance to escape, you shouldn't help them? If I see a man being physically assaulted, but he's in a situation where he could run away, I shouldn't help him? Seems to be a fairly questionable standard. &quot;Don't help if the victim can get away.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who exactly was the victim that Richard Spencer holding down and preventing from &quot;escaping&quot; from the interview he was giving on TV? Who was he assaulting? Because if he was doing that then sure, he deserved to get punched. But it was pretty clear that that was not the case, there was no victim in the area unable to escape, for which someone needed to intervene and protect. It was in the middle of the street with dozens of people walking past him. Anybody who didn't like being near him or didn't like what he was saying had ample opportunity to simply walk away, as you saw so many people do.<br /> <br /> So yes. If nobody is being assaulted, nobody is being physically hurt, nobody is being held against their will, the guy isn't ranting and raving, just answering a few questions, and everyone can simply walk away, then sorry but, you can't run over and start punching him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040412#post1040412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Richard Spencer (and many of his ilk) like showing up to counter-&quot;protest&quot; and disrupt others by spewing their hate speech. So Spencer should be able to shut down other people's gatherings by forcing them to either endure his hate, or walk away? I'm not seeing the compelling moral stance here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does Richard Spencer physically assault people in order to stop their protests? If so then returning the favor would be okay. But if all he's doing is saying mean, vile words, other people should come to his rallies and choose to shout him down with equally mean, vile words, just the same as he does. But they shouldn't be using physical violence to silence him (and likewise he shouldn't be using physical violence to assault other people). Other than punching him, people in this particular case had the option of yelling and screaming to ruin his interview.<br /> <br /> Of course, if he is physically assaulting people, hopefully the police arrest him and put him in prison.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040412#post1040412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming you mean, do I think it would be right to punch Spencer while he was minding his own business on the street (and assuming he's not wearing racist pins/etc. as he pretty much constantly does)? Probably not. Would I think there's a moral case for, say, disrupting one of his interviews so he doesn't get yet another public platform for his hate speech? Absolutely.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if someone is doing something you feel is traumatic to the well-being of other people (but isn't illegal), using violence to prevent them from using a public platform to share their beliefs is absolutely okay?<br /> <br /> To go back to my earlier statement on abortion - if someone is very pro-Life and they honestly believe that abortion is traumatic to the well-being of other people (since they believe it's literally killing people) even if it is legal, it would be morally acceptable for them to use violence in order to prevent people who are a pro-Choice from using a public platform to try to convince more people to believe that abortion is okay?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-30-2017, 01:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T00:07:53-08:00","id":1040472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1040421#post1040421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who exactly was the victim that Richard Spencer holding down and preventing from &quot;escaping&quot; from the interview he was giving on TV?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're dodging the question. Richard Spencer doesn't matter to the moral rule you suggested (that the victim as a moral duty to escape, and if they don't take it then they don't deserve protection by others).<br /> <br /> You keep trying to pick apart what I'm saying with various examples/hypothetical/etc., but when you get challenged in the same way, you just go, &quot;But Richard Spencer!&quot; as if that somehow was the sole ethical point of discussion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Who was he assaulting? </div> </div> </div>You do realize that assault as a crime does not have anything to do with actual physical contact. Regardless of the court's ruling to the contrary, I consider anyone that publicly advocates for genocide (even if he couches it in fancy dressing to make it sound better; &quot;peaceful genocide&quot; is an oxymoron) as attempting assault on the targets of that genocide, because they're trying to create apprehension of imminent violence or offensive contact. Assault doesn't have to have the intent to carry out the action, just the intent to cause the feeling of apprehension in the target.<br /> <br /> He wants non-whites and non-Christians to be afraid, constantly, to try to terrorize them with apprehension to drive them out of the country to maintain is stance that he doesn't want to actually kill anyone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If so then returning the favor would be okay. </div> </div> </div>We've been here before. We've established that physical violence is not out of bounds to defend against non-physical violence. Yet you run right back to arguments that rely on the on contrary.<br /> <br /> There's no ethical consistency to your responses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course, if he is physically assaulting people, hopefully the police arrest him and put him in prison. </div> </div> </div>He doesn't do that, because that would void the loopholes in the law he uses to perpetuate his hate without having to face consequences. He incites others to do it in a sleek fashion the law allows, so followers can go to jail and the leadership stays constant to create new followers.<br /> <br /> If he was a mob boss, he'd be rotting in jail, because RICO laws were designed specifically to keep organized crime from exploiting exactly this sort of thing. But perpetuating hate speech, as long as you don't run afoul of the Brandenburg rule means you're not committing a crime to punish him using those rules. There's plenty of guys in jail that didn't actually do any of the crimes they're charged with, because they were the leaders that set them in motion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So if someone is doing something you feel is traumatic to the well-being of other people (but isn't illegal), using violence to prevent them from using a public platform to share their beliefs is absolutely okay? </div> </div> </div>I said disruption is absolutely OK.<br /> <br /> Violence is variable. I actually think he's been in situations that are far more deserving of physical violence despite the law (pretty much any of his public rallies because they're designed to inspire fear and apprehension in the targets of his genocide) compared to him just being at someone else's event as a private citizen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To go back to my earlier statement on abortion </div> </div> </div>Nope. I addressed this and you haven't responded to what I said about it, so I'm not going to let you jump past that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T00:35:20-08:00","id":1040479,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://scontent.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/16388076_10155020322348000_2959781676352395001_n.jpg?oh=d5b586c40037c724453ac90c3cde56d8&amp;oe=5905A4C9\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Note that Richard Spencer absolutely qualifies as &quot;credible threat&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T05:24:30-08:00","id":1040577,"title":"","content":"Death threats or threats of violence and blackmail aren't freedom of speech, but one has to be careful the one doesn't get into the habit of silencing people who happen to simple offend your sensibilities, there is a line. <br /> <br /> And if someone does make a threat, but doesn't commit an act of violence, there is no excuse to punch them, call the police and let them handle it, this isn't the wild west and vigilantism is dangerous to society and a slippery slope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"