ral/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1080064#post1080064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do admire Hellboy's reaction times when it comes to the subject<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <img src=\"https://cdn.bleedingcool.net/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/CcCaFfTUUAAddP1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> In reality, that's something I thought about a lot.<br /> <br /> I had not the luck to meet my grandpa, cancer got him before I was even around, but something came through. See, he fought Nazis and Fascists when the rest of the country disagreed with him. When the neighbours sold him to the Fascist police and he got out when his family corrupted the officers to let him go? He went back fighting. When the Nazis beat down my great-grandmother to get to him? He left the town and went back fighting.. After getting out a prisoner's camp? Still went back fighting. He was also enough of a wise man to explain my father why he did what he did and let him decide if that was the right thing to do on his own. I do like to think I get the point as well.<br /> <br /> Violence is not a good thing. I'd never do it if given the choice. But, while I Free Speech is a big deal for me, I can't avoid thinking that when a rethoric is undeniably based on things like hate, hurting others or denying other people their right to live a peaceful life because of whatever reason motivates such rethoric, then the ones that follow it should be stopped before the damage is done.<br /> <br /> If you ask me, if there's the chance I can avoid bad stuff to happen and avoid sufference for those that never asked for it only by punching a Nazi (or a variant) today, I'd say it's a fair price. I'd compromise my own morality anytime if that avoids other people getting hurt. There's a point after what you preach becomes so toxic it has no right to be.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Freedom of Speech&amp;quot; is something that comes only after an even more fundamental right: the &amp;quot;Freedom to Be&amp;quot;. If you don't grant the latter to everyone, you lose the benefits of the former</div> </div> </div> </div>Couldn't have articulated it better. It's a tough subject, to be sure. Violence ISN'T a good thing, but I stand behind this argument completely. It and it's perfectly complimentary Hellboy reference. My morality is something I'd gladly compromise to protect my fellow human beings from needless suffering, at the hands of the hateful or in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T00:02:28-07:00","id":1080200,"title":"","content":"I don't think you have to consider it a compromise of your morality. Unless you follow a very strict absolutist ethical philosophy, there's nothing wrong or compromising about a moral code that accepts &quot;ranking&quot; of good and bad actions. If your moral principles say punching someone - despite violence being immoral - is better than not punching them, then you punch them and deal with the consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T00:35:45-07:00","id":1080771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1080200#post1080200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you have to consider it a compromise of your morality. Unless you follow a very strict absolutist ethical philosophy, there's nothing wrong or compromising about a moral code that accepts &amp;quot;ranking&amp;quot; of good and bad actions. If your moral principles say punching someone - despite violence being immoral - is better than not punching them, then you punch them and deal with the consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems to be a logical argument. Honestly, I've personally used what I would perceive as justifiable violence already. It's not uncommon for the bullied to punch back. Whether Nazi, homophobe, sadistic asshole, or whatever label the truly offending (and offensive) party uses to identify their douchebag selves, fighting fire with fire isn't an inherently bad thing to me. It's just not an inherently good thing, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T01:07:30-07:00","id":1080778,"title":"","content":"Yeah.<br /> <br /> I don't mean to aim this at anyone in particular, or mean it as a negative thing, but I think most people operate on something I call pragmatic unexamined utilitarianism. Or more simply, they judge morality on the basis of maximizing good impacts of what they do, and minimizing bad impacts of what they do. Most people don't study philosophy in-depth enough to really get into defining a specific ethical framework and interpretation they adhere to (and lots of those that do kinds suck at it, see: Kant). While I hesitate to call any sort of morality &quot;natural&quot; it's also a key determination in the biological definition of altruism (though that is phrased as benefit to other instead of good, and harm to self instead of bad, and is modified heavily by relation to the subject of your action).<br /> <br /> The point I'm trying to make is that the wide-spread belief in justification for bad actions as morally acceptable stems from the generalized concept that doing minor harm for a greater good. Which is why so many of us also feel comfortable punching Nazis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T20:50:13-07:00","id":1081269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1080778#post1080778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point I'm trying to make is that the wide-spread belief in justification for bad actions as morally acceptable stems from the generalized concept that doing minor harm for a greater good. Which is why so many of us also feel comfortable punching Nazis.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bUnfortunately, the definition of 'Nazi' in some minds has decayed to 'person that doesn't agree with me on something' with little regard to what they actually were and what they represented, and all too often is being used to justify the person's own Nazi-like behavior of using violence to shut down opposing views.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T22:16:20-07:00","id":1081296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1081269#post1081269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bUnfortunately, the definition of 'Nazi' in some minds has decayed to 'person that doesn't agree with me on something' with little regard to what they actually were and what they represented, and all too often is being used to justify the person's own Nazi-like behavior of using violence to shut down opposing views.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that I don't think there are a few assholes using &quot;they're a nazi&quot; as justification to punch people, but that's not what happened in the case being discussed here, Richard Spencer. He is, in fact, a neo-nazi, or at the very least, a white supremacist (I don't care if he wants to call it &quot;identitarian&quot; or whatever, if you advocate in favor of ethnic cleansing for the sake of creating a homeland for the sake of the &quot;dispossessed white race&quot; you are engaging in white supremacist advocacy). We can argue all day about whether or not his being a white supremacist justifies punching him in and of itself, but arguing he's just a &quot;person who disagrees with me on something&quot; is disingenuous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T22:57:13-07:00","id":1081312,"title":"","content":"Yes.<br /> <br /> I revived the thread with the, 'They're going to hit someone' comment because of the recent actions at Berkeley, where a neo-Nazi punched a protester. Said Neo-Nazi is also part of a larger student organization attempting to spread the word at campuses across the nation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T14:25:07-07:00","id":1081580,"title":"","content":"There seems to be this disturbing tendency to try rebranding the advocation of the persecution of people as a &quot;freedom.&quot; Like say the religious &quot;freedom&quot; bills being pushed in various places around the States. Probably more palatable to the people who think about voting for those things that the uncomfortable thought that the &quot;freedom&quot; being advocated is the marginalization socially, economically, medically,etc of historically persecuted groups. If you find yourself wanting to toe the letter, not the spirit of concepts of free speech to such degrees of absurdity then you don't really advocate for free speech at all. I can't respect people that take it that far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T16:42:48-07:00","id":1081624,"title":"","content":"As a non-Christian person of faith in the US, every time I hear of &quot;religious freedom&quot; legislation, I know that it's bullshit because if does anything to protect my religion's beliefs or practices, it will be completely coincidental, and usually such bills infringe on my religion more than they offer protections for it.<br /> <br /> I'll consider giving a shit about the &quot;War on Christmas&quot; when I don't lose multiple days of vacation time a year because my holidays aren't automatic days off for everyone. But that is one of the core problems in the US. The response to try to make society more respectful to everyone is to treat it as an attack on the majority.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T17:25:01-07:00","id":1081640,"title":"","content":"There's also a lot of anti-intellectualism around the world. 'Don't listen to some fancy university professor, it's the freedom act, it's good for freedom, if you're against it, you're against freedom.'<br /> <br /> But this is, again, another derailment from people punching Nazis and Nazis punching people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-20-2017, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T05:21:35-07:00","id":1083409,"title":"","content":"I don't know much about Richard Spencer, but seems to me most people being attacked by antifa folks are just regular old cultural conservatives or classical liberals, definitely can't condone punching them. Secular Talk has an interesting video on this topic:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=E5KJo4v3TXs\" data-code=\"E5KJo4v3TXs\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/E5KJo4v3TXs/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Honestly, even if there are some Nazi's it's really not a problem like it was back in the day, when they tried to take over the world and were supported by big-business/military. If we are going to be allowed to punch people it is best to go after the threats of the 21st century rather than the early 20th.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11522-the_1990","name":"the_1990","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T20:36:34-07:00","id":1083801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the_1990</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1083409#post1083409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know much about Richard Spencer, but seems to me most people being attacked by antifa folks are just regular old cultural conservatives or classical liberals, definitely can't condone punching them. Secular Talk has an interesting video on this topic:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=E5KJo4v3TXs\" data-code=\"E5KJo4v3TXs\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/E5KJo4v3TXs/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Honestly, even if there are some Nazi's it's really not a problem like it was back in the day, when they tried to take over the world and were supported by big-business/military. If we are going to be allowed to punch people it is best to go after the threats of the 21st century rather than the early 20th.</div> </div> </div> </div>The sort of neofascists that people are currently punching are not the people of the 20th century. Which I feel sort of odd to point out because it's a matter of chronological obviousness. Likewise the nature of these things in terms of different countries is what is being confronted. Not the ghost of an evil who has unfortunately maintained some legacy.<br /> <br /> And side note. My earlier comment was not a derailment, it was comment directly to the various actions and reactions currently playing out in the U.S. and elsewhere over this very issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T11:05:34-07:00","id":1084067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the_1990</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1083409#post1083409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If we are going to be allowed to punch people it is best to go after the threats of the 21st century rather than the early 20th.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you care to elaborate further on what the punchable threats of the 21st century are?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","user":"Caitiff Primogen","date":". 04-26-2017, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T12:54:15-07:00","id":1084107,"title":"","content":"I'm also curious about how the &quot;punchable&quot; threats of the 21st century compare to the political movements of the late 19th/early 20th centuries that spawned the specific Nazi movement.<br /> <br /> I think a lot of us worried about Nazis now are worried because it seems like the geopolitical stage is primed for a similar situation that opened the door for the Nazis to take power in Germany and all the consequences that had.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T13:13:52-07:00","id":1084122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1084107#post1084107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a lot of us worried about Nazis now are worried because it seems like the geopolitical stage is primed for a similar situation that opened the door for the Nazis to take power in Germany and all the consequences that had.</div> </div> </div> </div>And some of us are looking around for people likely to start a fire in the Reichstag. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T13:30:58-07:00","id":1084127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1084107#post1084107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also curious about how the &amp;quot;punchable&amp;quot; threats of the 21st century compare to the political movements of the late 19th/early 20th centuries that spawned the specific Nazi movement.<br /> <br /> I think a lot of us worried about Nazis now are worried because it seems like the geopolitical stage is primed for a similar situation that opened the door for the Nazis to take power in Germany and all the consequences that had.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm having a lot of difficulty in seeing how the United States is in a similar situation as Germany was after the Great War under the Treaty of Versailles...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T14:21:56-07:00","id":1084153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1084067#post1084067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you care to elaborate further on what the punchable threats of the 21st century are?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm choosing my words carefully here, as I don't want someone to misinterpret what I write and get me banned:<br /> <br /> Ideally no one should be victimised by mob violence, as the government should be stepping in to protect people, as the governments of the USA, USSR and UK protected the world from the Axis in WWII.<br /> <br /> There are two threats in the modern era comparable to the Axis: Islamic extremism and wealth inequality.<br /> <br /> Both are insidious and driven by human actors. Both, as I see it, threaten to overwhelm the current world order and change it for the worse, one seeks to create an oppressive theocracy and the other will have us all living in some nightmarish post-industrial feudalism.<br /> <br /> Again, I think getting the government to deal with these problems is infinitely preferable to mob violence, but these things have caused me a great deal of worry as I have become more politically aware. If it's now OK to punch people, it should be the ones who actively want to kill or enslave us right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11522-the_1990","name":"the_1990","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T14:34:26-07:00","id":1084161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1084107#post1084107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also curious about how the &quot;punchable&quot; threats of the 21st century compare to the political movements of the late 19th/early 20th centuries that spawned the specific Nazi movement.<br /> <br /> I think a lot of us worried about Nazis now are worried because it seems like the geopolitical stage is primed for a similar situation that opened the door for the Nazis to take power in Germany and all the consequences that had.</div> </div> </div> </div>What made the Nazis and fascists so dangerous was because they were supported by big businesses and military leadership, the Franco nationalists in Spain were able to seize power because so many officers in the Spanish military sympathised with them. Businesses in the west also supported them with weapons and funding while western governments didn't do enough to help the republicans.<br /> <br /> 1930s fascism was basically an unholy alliance between corporatism and militarism, they used misplaced populist rage as a weapon to destroy communism and ensure that the people didn't become too sympathetic to pacifism. It's no coincidence that Hitler was in such a hurry to invade the USSR before he had even beaten the western allies, or that pacifism was relentlessly attacked (Nazis once released rats into theatres screening antiwar films.)<br /> <br /> This unholy alliance still exists today, only it's now called neo-conservatism.<br /> <br /> Even if the 21st century's right wing populists were exactly the same as the NAZI's (they aren't, really) they don't have the support of those powerful institutions which originally allowed them to almost take over the world","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11522-the_1990","name":"the_1990","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T15:51:37-07:00","id":1084194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1084127#post1084127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm having a lot of difficulty in seeing how the United States is in a similar situation as Germany was after the Great War under the Treaty of Versailles...</div> </div> </div> </div>Never said the US was going to be where this happens. However the US is already culturally engaging in all of the things that made us complacent in the atrocities of WWII (including the ones we committed).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the_1990</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1084153#post1084153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are two threats in the modern era comparable to the Axis: Islamic extremism and wealth inequality.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems... woefully misguided.<br /> <br /> Islamist terrorism is, in terms of actual impact, a red herring to justify jingoist posturing. It is a bad thing, it should be stopped, but it is not a threat to the peaceful global order. We posture against it because it's a threat to the Islamic theocratic human rights hating governments that play nice with the rest of the world (Saudi Arabia, Kuwait, Qatar, UAE, etc.) that provide us natural resources, not because it's any real danger to the functioning of Christian majority nations.<br /> <br /> Wealth inequality is a bigger danger to democratic humanist ideology, but it's only dangerous as a factor in a great number of other issues.<br /> <br /> The Western trend of anti-intellectualism and anti-establishment politics is a far bigger existential threat, because it undermines the institutions put in place after WWII to keep that from happening again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the_1990</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1084161#post1084161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What made the Nazis and fascists so dangerous was because they were supported by big businesses and military leadership, the Franco nationalists in Spain were able to seize power because so many officers in the Spanish military sympathised with them. Businesses in the west also supported them with weapons and funding while western governments didn't do enough to help the republicans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right... so... have you seen Trumps cabinet and advisors? Or Putin's political allies?<br /> <br /> The military industrial complex is pretty much as powerful as ever, and there's a lot of support in it for a lot of very nasty views. The ultimate reason ISIS has managed to do as much damage as it has, is because of the same things you're pointing at that screwed up Spain in the 30s.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1930s fascism was basically an unholy alliance between corporatism and militarism, they used misplaced populist rage as a weapon to destroy communism and ensure that the people didn't become too sympathetic to pacifism. </div> </div> </div>And 2010s fascism is going down the same rabbit hole but targeting the global institutions like the UN, EU, NATO, and so on that want to restrain military force, and use a new set of minority scapegoats to use to justify massive increases in military spending.<br /> <br /> And really, if your argument here is that the forces that lead to Nazi Germany are only significantly different because they have less backing from institutions, that's hardly comforting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T16:13:59-07:00","id":1084198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1038569-violence-begets-violence?p=1084194#post1084194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Never said the US was going to be where this happens. However the US is already culturally engaging in all of the things that made us complacent in the atrocities of WWII (including the ones we committed).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This seems... woefully misguided.<br /> <br /> Islamist terrorism is, in terms of actual impact, a red herring to justify jingoist posturing. It is a bad thing, it should be stopped, but it is not a threat to the peaceful global order. We posture against it because it's a threat to the Islamic theocratic human rights hating governments that play nice with the rest of the world (Saudi Arabia, Kuwait, Qatar, UAE, etc.) that provide us natural resources, not because it's any real danger to the functioning of Christian majority nations.<br /> <br /> Wealth inequality is a bigger danger to democratic humanist ideology, but it's only dangerous as a factor in a great number of other issues.<br /> <br /> The Western trend of anti-intellectualism and anti-establishment politics is a far bigger existential threat, because it undermines the institutions put in place after WWII to keep that from happening again.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Right... so... have you seen Trumps cabinet and advisors? Or Putin's political allies?<br /> <br /> The military industrial complex is pretty much as powerful as ever, and there's a lot of support in it for a lot of very nasty views. The ultimate reason ISIS has managed to do as much damage as it has, is because of the same things you're pointing at that screwed up Spain in the 30s.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And 2010s fascism is going down the same rabbit hole but targeting the global institutions like the UN, EU, NATO, and so on that want to restrain military force, and use a new set of minority scapegoats to use to justify massive increases in military spending.<br /> <br /> And really, if your argument here is that the forces that lead to Nazi Germany are only significantly different because they have less backing from institutions, that's hardly comforting.</div> </div> </div> </div>What Heavy Arms said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}